istency","title":"Fresh whole-artifact consistency and finding reconciliation","selectors":[],"concerns":["Reconcile all substantive reviews against the originating ISSUE, applicable prior design, stakeholder evidence and repository conventions.","Check indirect effects on unchanged requirements, interfaces, ownership, dependencies and consumer behavior.","Reconcile prompt guarantees, retry cooldowns, migration and recovery claims across canonical content, live document, acceptance mapping and generated visual.","Reassess every carried finding using fresh evidence without treating revision intent as resolution.","Keep demonstrated defects, mandatory verification limitations and optional advice distinct, and apply the required status precedence."],"dependsOn":["scope","vault","runtime","visuals"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 33 current inventory units are assigned to substantive chunks. Contracts, data-model changes, error handling and tests are shared between vault and runtime so each implementation responsibility retains its complete behavior and verification scope. Citation indices reflect the newly inserted run-file reference and added stakeholder citation. The diagram document selector moves from line 191 to line 208. Every substantive chunk receives fresh review; final consistency depends on all four and does not substitute for inventory coverage.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["vault","runtime"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["vault","runtime"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["vault","runtime"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["vault","runtime"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["vault"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/companions","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["vault","runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["vault"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/7","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/8","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/9","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/10","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"document:line:25","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"document:line:208","chunkIds":["visuals"]}]},"impact":{"baselineAttempt":1,"mode":"full","changes":["Summary and alternatives now cite stakeholder decision A accepting legacy-item migration prompts and possible additional save prompts; a stakeholder citation is added.","Vault contracts now specify a shared mutation queue, per-name legacy single-flight and cached value, absence and failure states, with save/delete invalidation and pre-copy state rechecks.","Payload validation now covers the complete version-1 shape, unique retired names, disjoint membership and arbitrary account names stored in a Map.","A maintenance lifetime guard and daemon pre-load conflict check are introduced, with new ownership errors and a run-file API citation.","Unit and integration strategies add migration interleavings, malformed payloads, repeated failed-copy reads, process guard scenarios and backend injection below the vault through process preloads.","Migration now describes stale-value recovery, loss of new secrets and possible resurrection of deleted secrets, and changes rollbackability labels.","The sequence now distinguishes copied vault contents from legacy reads and migration writes; participant descriptions and generated companion content change.","The diagram section moves from document line 191 to line 208; citation indices 7 and 8 change referents, and indices 9 and 10 are added."],"directChunkIds":["scope","vault","runtime","visuals"],"indirectChunkIds":[],"rationale":"Attempt 1 is the immediately preceding completed review execution, with a complete publication record, although its assessment status is incomplete because actual diagram rendering was unavailable. Checkpoint provenance identifies both attempts as daemon/gpt-6.1-sol. Comparison of its captured baseline with the current canonical artifact and live document shows direct changes in every substantive responsibility, so full mode is warranted without retaining any prior coverage. The scope exception affects the unchanged ISSUE requirement and acceptance interpretation; new migration states affect unchanged consumers and public signatures; the guard depends on existing daemon socket publication and maintenance admission ordering; backend injection must work across those ownership boundaries. Unchanged context, chosenAlternative, openQuestions, interactionWithShared and companion path must therefore be reconsidered with their changed dependencies. Fresh visual inspection must retry the outstanding rendering verification. All eight effective findings are carried for reassessment, with none resolved during preparation.","chunkMapping":[{"priorIds":["scope"],"currentIds":["scope"],"explanation":"Responsibility remains issue traceability and architectural choice. Upstream citations move from indices 7/8 to 8/9, and decision A adds index 10. Changed prompt exceptions require fresh assessment."},{"priorIds":["vault"],"currentIds":["vault"],"explanation":"Responsibility remains vault contracts, migration, errors and unit verification. Mutation ordering, per-name states, validation, recovery and tests changed; no coverage is retained."},{"priorIds":["runtime"],"currentIds":["runtime"],"explanation":"Responsibility remains lifecycle, consumers and ownership, now explicitly including the new global maintenance guard and citation 7. Changed exclusion and injection contracts require fresh review of unchanged entry points and dependencies."},{"priorIds":["visuals"],"currentIds":["visuals"],"explanation":"Responsibility remains sequence source and generated rendering. The document selector changes from line 191 to 208, sequence behavior changes, and prior rendering verification was incomplete."},{"priorIds":["consistency"],"currentIds":["consistency"],"explanation":"The final consistency responsibility and dependency topology are preserved, but the result must be freshly produced after all current substantive reviews."}],"retainedCoverage":[],"carriedFindingIds":["[1,\"scope\",\"scope-001\"]","[1,\"vault\",\"vault-001\"]","[1,\"vault\",\"vault-002\"]","[1,\"vault\",\"vault-003\"]","[1,\"vault\",\"vault-004\"]","[1,\"runtime\",\"runtime-001\"]","[1,\"runtime\",\"runtime-002\"]","[1,\"visuals\",\"visuals-001\"]"],"consistencyChunkIds":["consistency"]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"impact","phase":"impact","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"vault","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"runtime","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"visuals","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":2,"retriesUsed":1,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Resolution requires accepted fresh inspection without mandatory gaps"}],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1","attempt":2,"artifactId":"LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":4,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The LLD restores the originating issue’s full scope, preserves standalone ancestry, and carries forward applicable constraints from the prior LLD. Decision A records migration and save exceptions, but the claimed lifetime migration-prompt bound contradicts the specified retry behavior.","findings":[{"id":"scope-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/summary; /body/alternativesConsidered/0/cons","message":"The design promises that each legacy item prompts only once in its lifetime, but its failure behavior cannot preserve that bound. When a legacy read succeeds and its vault copy fails, the value is cached only for the current run and migration retries next run. If access was granted with Allow, that next legacy read can prompt again. A refused legacy read also retries after five minutes. Citation c11 records acceptance of a prompt when first copying each item, without addressing these repeated attempts, while openQuestions is empty. Qualify the lifetime claim to successful migration and explicitly reconcile retry prompts with the accepted exception, including corresponding acceptance coverage.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:11 — once-in-a-lifetime migration exception","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:236 — failed copy caches the value this run and retries next run","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:240 — refused legacy reads retry after five minutes","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:313 — repeats the lifetime prompt bound",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json — /citations/10 and /body/openQuestions","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md — Expected behavior and Fix intent 2"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:25","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/10","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261105669ae7a3/S001/LLD.md","src/shared/keystore.ts","src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts","src/daemon/index.ts:470","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts","node_modules/keytar/src/keytar_mac.cc"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"vault","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected all assigned vault selectors against the originating issue, canonical artifact and current consumers. Mutation serialization, migration caching, retirement and recovery losses are now specified. Runtime mutation validation remains a gap that can turn one malformed IPC save into an unreadable consolidated vault.","findings":[{"id":"vault-005","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/1; /body/dataModelChanges/0; /body/testStrategy","message":"The design validates the complete payload only on load, but does not require runtime validation of mutation arguments or the candidate payload before persistence. Current keys.set handlers merely cast unknown IPC params; keytar currently rejects non-string account/password arguments. Consolidation removes that protection because keytar receives fixed service/account strings and a serialized JSON string. For example, keys.set with {name:\"brave\",value:42} can persist a numeric secret under the specified write rules, then make the entire vault fail validation on restart, blocking unrelated credentials. Require runtime name/value validation at the vault owner boundary, or equivalent candidate-payload validation before every write, and test malformed IPC saves/deletes leave both memory and persisted content unchanged.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:58 — setKey specifies TypeScript arguments and persistence ordering without runtime input validation","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:141 — whole-payload validation occurs on load and rejects non-string secret values","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474 — keys.set casts params and passes name/value directly to setKey","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1488 — keys.delete likewise relies on a TypeScript cast","src/daemon/server.ts:95 — directDispatch passes request.params to the handler without method-specific validation","node_modules/keytar/src/main.cc:17 — existing native boundary rejects non-string usernames","node_modules/keytar/src/main.cc:25 — existing native boundary rejects non-string passwords",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json — /body/testStrategy/testLevels/0 covers malformed stored payloads, but not malformed mutation inputs"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/1","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261105669ae7a3/S001/LLD.md","src/shared/keystore.ts","src/daemon/db/secrets.ts","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474","src/daemon/server.ts","src/daemon/tools/config.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/notify/index.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/web/index.ts","src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts","node_modules/keytar/lib/keytar.js","node_modules/keytar/src/main.cc"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Add explicit listKeys compatibility tests for unmigrated, migrated, failed-copy-cached, retired and restored names; the current enumeration test checks only that findCredentials is not called.","Explicitly include duplicate retired names and overlapping secrets/retired membership in malformed-payload fixtures, matching the newly stated validation contract.","The current scope review already records the lifetime migration-prompt contradiction as scope-002. Apply its qualification consistently to migration step 3 and distinguish immediate repository-open retries from Keychain retries after the cooldown."]},{"chunkId":"runtime","status":"passed","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the originating ISSUE, applicable prior LLD and current runtime code. The proposed lifecycle, main-thread vault ownership, maintenance guard and below-vault test injection are feasible. No additional blocking defect was demonstrated within this assignment.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/citations/0","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261105669ae7a3/S001/LLD.md","src/shared/keystore.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts","src/shared/daemon-process.ts","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts","src/cli/services/connection-maintenance.ts","src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts","src/daemon/db/management-tickets.ts","src/daemon/db/management.ts","src/daemon/db/management-adoption.ts","src/daemon/db/secrets.ts","src/daemon/db/pool-cache.ts","src/daemon/db/__tests__/management-defaults.test.ts","src/daemon/connection-management-rpc.ts","src/daemon/connection-session-rpc.ts","src/daemon/db-rpc.ts","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474","src/daemon/index.ts:468","src/daemon/index.ts:596","src/daemon/server.ts:283","src/daemon/shutdown.ts","src/daemon/run-file-ownership.ts","src/daemon/threads/channel.ts","src/daemon/threads/main-services.ts:207","src/daemon/threads/worker-entry.ts:66","src/daemon/threads/session-worker.ts:57","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:73","src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts:368","src/daemon/tools/config.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/notify/index.ts:18","src/daemon/tools/builtins/web/index.ts:68","node_modules/keytar/src/async.cc"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Expand integration subjects to exercise owner, safeList, legacy listing and save independently; include threads-disabled operation, unrelated-request progress during a held read, repository isolation, concurrent maintenance admission and orphan-guard recovery. The current generic first-management-request subject could exercise capabilities alone.","Specify the hub operation payloads and forwarder error reconstruction explicitly. src/daemon/threads/channel.ts currently transports ordinary errors as name/message-only HubRemoteError instances and drops their cause; the forwarder should deliberately produce the promised KeystoreUnavailableError without worker-local fallback.","Clarify the retry test wording: an immediate request after denial retries the repository opener but receives the cached vault failure; Keychain access retries only after the five-minute cooldown.","Retain the prior LLD's explicit distinction between ticket-key, rollback-copy and connection-secret failures in integration assertions, including fixed client messages and unchanged recovery handling for missing secrets."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"Inspected the complete sequence definition, all four participants, and generated companion source. The companion preserves the authored messages and descriptions, but its legacy-path conditions conflict with the vault contracts. Actual rendering could not be verified.","findings":[{"id":"visuals-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/sequenceDefinition/messages/4-6","message":"The legacy branch is guarded only by the name being absent from the vault. This also includes retired names and names with cached legacy results, for which the contracts prohibit another legacy lookup. The following copy message additionally lacks the condition that a legacy value was found, although the preceding return explicitly permits no value. The generated companion repeats these conditions. Specify that fallback requires a non-retired name without a reusable run result, and that persistence requires a found value plus the mutation-queue recheck. Otherwise the sequence directs unnecessary Keychain access for deleted or cached names and a write for an absent name, contradicting the deletion and no-write guarantees.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition/messages/4, /5 and /6","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded Mermaid steps 5–7 and corresponding Messages descriptions","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:161 — cached, absent and retired-name rules","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:258 — absent lookup causes no write","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:261 — retired names must not fall back"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/companions","document:line:208","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts","src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts","src/shared/keystore.ts"],"limitations":["Mandatory rendered inspection of /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html could not be completed: opening the companion through the browser tool returned 'The browser access host is unavailable'. Source and retained descriptions were inspected; layout, readability and successful diagram rendering remain unverified."],"advice":["Consider extending the sequence with the main-thread on-demand management-opening path and annotating the mutually exclusive offline maintenance owner. Those boundaries are described in the surrounding contracts but are outside this diagram's stated secret-read scope.","Clarify the Keychain participant description: legacy items remain after successful copying until explicitly deleted, rather than existing only 'until copied'."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"Reconciled the current LLD, originating ISSUE, applicable prior design, canonical content, generated companion source and all four accepted substantive reviews. Six prior findings are resolved by freshly inspected contracts; the scope finding is superseded by the current prompt-bound finding. The prior visual finding remains carried because fresh visual inspection has a mandatory rendering gap. Current substantive findings require changes; unavailable rendered verification makes the overall consistency result incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261105669ae7a3/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html","src/shared/keystore.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474","src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts","node_modules/keytar/src/main.cc"],"limitations":["Mandatory rendered verification of /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html remains incomplete. The accepted fresh visuals chunk reports that browser access failed with 'The browser access host is unavailable'. This consistency inspection verified the embedded Mermaid and description tables, which cannot establish successful rendering, layout or readability. Consequently, visuals-001 cannot be resolved or superseded using the incomplete fresh visual inspection."],"advice":["Retain current findings scope-002, vault-005 and visuals-002 without duplicating them here. They respectively cover contradictory migration prompt bounds, malformed mutation inputs capable of corrupting the consolidated vault, and legacy sequence conditions inconsistent with retirement and cached-result contracts.","Apply scope-002 consistently to the summary, alternative a1, migration step 3, sequence narrative and generated message descriptions. Distinguish successful migration from failed-copy retries on later runs and refused-read retries after five minutes.","The repository opener's immediate retry and the keystore's five-minute cooldown can coexist: an immediate request retries opening but receives the cached keystore failure. Make this distinction explicit in the integration subject and acceptance mapping.","Preserve the runtime review's optional coverage recommendations for individual management entry points, unrelated-request progress, repository isolation and guard recovery. Preserve the vault review's enumeration and malformed-payload fixture recommendations.","The prior narrowed LLD supplies applicable lifecycle and error-handling constraints, but its earlier scope split does not limit this full-scope replacement. Decision A now records the migration and save exceptions; scope-002 identifies the remaining inconsistency in their stated bound."],"findingDecisions":[{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-001"},"rationale":"Fresh scope inspection confirms that citation c11 and the summary now explicitly capture stakeholder decision A accepting legacy migration and save prompts. This addresses the original absence of an authorized exception. The remaining inaccurate lifetime bound is assessed by the real current replacement scope-002.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: /citations/10 and /body/summary","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:11",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks scope, scope-002; limitations empty"],"action":"superseded","reviewedInChunkIds":["scope"],"supersededBy":{"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-002"}},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-001"},"rationale":"The current design puts migration copies, saves and deletes in one mutation queue, requires a fresh vault/retirement check before copying, and specifies per-name single-flight reads. Its test strategy now includes concurrent misses and migration interleavings with saves and deletes. Fresh vault inspection has no mandatory gaps.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:152","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:161","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-002"},"rationale":"Per-name run state now distinguishes in-flight lookup, copied value, cached value after failed persistence, absence and failed read with cooldown. Successful mutations clear the state. Repeated failed-copy reads and refused legacy-read cooldowns have explicit test subjects. This resolves the missing subsequent-read behavior.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:161","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:236","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-003"},"rationale":"Load validation now requires version 1, string-valued secrets, unique string retirement entries and disjoint membership. Map storage handles arbitrary account names, and malformed stored payloads have fail-closed test subjects. The current vault-005 concerns a distinct mutation-input boundary and does not invalidate resolution of this stored-payload validation defect.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:141","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:220","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-004"},"rationale":"Migration now explicitly describes abandonment as data-losing recovery, including loss of new secrets, reversion of changed legacy values and resurrection after failed legacy deletion. Steps 3 and 4 are marked non-rollbackable, with the mutation boundary caveat stated. Fresh vault inspection confirms the misleading recovery claims are corrected.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:187","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:313","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:314",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"runtime","findingId":"runtime-001"},"rationale":"The maintenance process now acquires the global guard before checking daemon control files and holds it through exit. Daemon vault loading occurs after socket publication and checks for that guard first. This ordering excludes simultaneous snapshots; atomic guard acquisition also excludes concurrent maintenance owners. Conflict, release and crash behavior are specified, with integration subjects. Fresh runtime inspection finds the protocol feasible without mandatory gaps.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:178","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:224","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:286","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts: acquireRunFileGuard and runFileGuardConflict",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks runtime"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["runtime"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"runtime","findingId":"runtime-002"},"rationale":"The test design replaces the above-vault database-port fixture with backend injection below the vault. A node --import preload installs it in spawned daemon and maintenance processes and rejects backend calls from workers. This exercises shared consumers and owner routing instead of bypassing the implementation. Fresh runtime inspection accepts its feasibility.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:282","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:285","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:287",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks runtime"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["runtime"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-001"},"rationale":"Current source qualifies the copied-name path and adds legacy messages, but the accepted fresh visuals inspection remains incomplete because rendering was unavailable. It also identifies incorrect legacy conditions as visuals-002. Preserve the prior origin unresolved rather than treating source revision intent or an inspection with mandatory gaps as sufficient resolution or supersession.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded Mermaid and Messages table",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks visuals, visuals-002 and rendering limitation"],"action":"carry"}]}],"limitations":["Mandatory rendered inspection of /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html could not be completed: opening the companion through the browser tool returned 'The browser access host is unavailable'. Source and retained descriptions were inspected; layout, readability and successful diagram rendering remain unverified.","Mandatory rendered verification of /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html remains incomplete. The accepted fresh visuals chunk reports that browser access failed with 'The browser access host is unavailable'. This consistency inspection verified the embedded Mermaid and description tables, which cannot establish successful rendering, layout or readability. Consequently, visuals-001 cannot be resolved or superseded using the incomplete fresh visual inspection."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"b9052f1142ff87b95aa661456e9b82210feb23ad1a54a9938abd7c82a54c7581","impact":{"baselineAttempt":1,"mode":"full","coverageOrigins":[{"chunkId":"scope","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"vault","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"runtime","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"visuals","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"consistency","kind":"fresh"}],"findingDecisions":[{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-001"},"rationale":"Fresh scope inspection confirms that citation c11 and the summary now explicitly capture stakeholder decision A accepting legacy migration and save prompts. This addresses the original absence of an authorized exception. The remaining inaccurate lifetime bound is assessed by the real current replacement scope-002.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: /citations/10 and /body/summary","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:11",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks scope, scope-002; limitations empty"],"action":"superseded","reviewedInChunkIds":["scope"],"supersededBy":{"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-002"}},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-001"},"rationale":"The current design puts migration copies, saves and deletes in one mutation queue, requires a fresh vault/retirement check before copying, and specifies per-name single-flight reads. Its test strategy now includes concurrent misses and migration interleavings with saves and deletes. Fresh vault inspection has no mandatory gaps.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:152","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:161","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-002"},"rationale":"Per-name run state now distinguishes in-flight lookup, copied value, cached value after failed persistence, absence and failed read with cooldown. Successful mutations clear the state. Repeated failed-copy reads and refused legacy-read cooldowns have explicit test subjects. This resolves the missing subsequent-read behavior.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:161","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:236","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-003"},"rationale":"Load validation now requires version 1, string-valued secrets, unique string retirement entries and disjoint membership. Map storage handles arbitrary account names, and malformed stored payloads have fail-closed test subjects. The current vault-005 concerns a distinct mutation-input boundary and does not invalidate resolution of this stored-payload validation defect.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:141","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:220","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-004"},"rationale":"Migration now explicitly describes abandonment as data-losing recovery, including loss of new secrets, reversion of changed legacy values and resurrection after failed legacy deletion. Steps 3 and 4 are marked non-rollbackable, with the mutation boundary caveat stated. Fresh vault inspection confirms the misleading recovery claims are corrected.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:187","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:313","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:314",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"runtime","findingId":"runtime-001"},"rationale":"The maintenance process now acquires the global guard before checking daemon control files and holds it through exit. Daemon vault loading occurs after socket publication and checks for that guard first. This ordering excludes simultaneous snapshots; atomic guard acquisition also excludes concurrent maintenance owners. Conflict, release and crash behavior are specified, with integration subjects. Fresh runtime inspection finds the protocol feasible without mandatory gaps.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:178","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:224","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:286","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts: acquireRunFileGuard and runFileGuardConflict",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks runtime"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["runtime"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"runtime","findingId":"runtime-002"},"rationale":"The test design replaces the above-vault database-port fixture with backend injection below the vault. A node --import preload installs it in spawned daemon and maintenance processes and rejects backend calls from workers. This exercises shared consumers and owner routing instead of bypassing the implementation. Fresh runtime inspection accepts its feasibility.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:282","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:285","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:287",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks runtime"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["runtime"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-001"},"rationale":"Current source qualifies the copied-name path and adds legacy messages, but the accepted fresh visuals inspection remains incomplete because rendering was unavailable. It also identifies incorrect legacy conditions as visuals-002. Preserve the prior origin unresolved rather than treating source revision intent or an inspection with mandatory gaps as sufficient resolution or supersession.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded Mermaid and Messages table",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks visuals, visuals-002 and rendering limitation"],"action":"carry"}],"effectiveFindingOrigins":[{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-001"},{"attempt":2,"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-002"},{"attempt":2,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-005"},{"attempt":2,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-002"}]}},"finishedAt":"2026-11-08T12:55:35.353Z"}],"applicableAttempt":2,"status":"incomplete","binding":{"sourceRevision":{"number":2,"contentHash":"e97f4687126f5e3b60e0983c01a71a92888845c3ba639c62be474f96b1ef87cf"},"reviewedContentIdentity":"b9052f1142ff87b95aa661456e9b82210feb23ad1a54a9938abd7c82a54c7581","documentDigest":"337c659409fa8d31614a1dccd955856b79b356db9e787de74fa6be86bd0cd9b0","workflowDigest":"be2abea3305056cc28af24014428b9bb300cf589fc8e48530415526529be87a5","author":"controller"},"preservationDigest":"1723a2dbbadf65ae95a324d631f33edd3881ea57616cb32a72637d815a6ecb3a"}}}}
