istency","title":"Fresh whole-artifact consistency and finding reconciliation","selectors":[],"concerns":["Reconcile all substantive reviews against the originating ISSUE, applicable prior design, stakeholder evidence and repository conventions.","Check indirect effects on unchanged requirements, interfaces, ownership, dependencies and consumer behavior.","Reconcile prompt guarantees, retry cooldowns, migration and recovery claims across canonical content, live document, acceptance mapping and generated visual.","Reassess every carried finding using fresh evidence without treating revision intent as resolution.","Keep demonstrated defects, mandatory verification limitations and optional advice distinct, and apply the required status precedence."],"dependsOn":["scope","vault","runtime","visuals"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 33 current inventory units are assigned to substantive chunks. Contracts, data-model changes, error handling and tests are shared between vault and runtime so each implementation responsibility retains its complete behavior and verification scope. Citation indices reflect the newly inserted run-file reference and added stakeholder citation. The diagram document selector moves from line 191 to line 208. Every substantive chunk receives fresh review; final consistency depends on all four and does not substitute for inventory coverage.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["vault","runtime"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["vault","runtime"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["vault","runtime"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["vault","runtime"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["vault"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/companions","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["vault","runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["vault"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/7","chunkIds":["runtime"]},{"unitId":"/citations/8","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/9","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/10","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"document:line:25","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"document:line:208","chunkIds":["visuals"]}]},"impact":{"baselineAttempt":1,"mode":"full","changes":["Summary and alternatives now cite stakeholder decision A accepting legacy-item migration prompts and possible additional save prompts; a stakeholder citation is added.","Vault contracts now specify a shared mutation queue, per-name legacy single-flight and cached value, absence and failure states, with save/delete invalidation and pre-copy state rechecks.","Payload validation now covers the complete version-1 shape, unique retired names, disjoint membership and arbitrary account names stored in a Map.","A maintenance lifetime guard and daemon pre-load conflict check are introduced, with new ownership errors and a run-file API citation.","Unit and integration strategies add migration interleavings, malformed payloads, repeated failed-copy reads, process guard scenarios and backend injection below the vault through process preloads.","Migration now describes stale-value recovery, loss of new secrets and possible resurrection of deleted secrets, and changes rollbackability labels.","The sequence now distinguishes copied vault contents from legacy reads and migration writes; participant descriptions and generated companion content change.","The diagram section moves from document line 191 to line 208; citation indices 7 and 8 change referents, and indices 9 and 10 are added."],"directChunkIds":["scope","vault","runtime","visuals"],"indirectChunkIds":[],"rationale":"Attempt 1 is the immediately preceding completed review execution, with a complete publication record, although its assessment status is incomplete because actual diagram rendering was unavailable. Checkpoint provenance identifies both attempts as daemon/gpt-6.1-sol. Comparison of its captured baseline with the current canonical artifact and live document shows direct changes in every substantive responsibility, so full mode is warranted without retaining any prior coverage. The scope exception affects the unchanged ISSUE requirement and acceptance interpretation; new migration states affect unchanged consumers and public signatures; the guard depends on existing daemon socket publication and maintenance admission ordering; backend injection must work across those ownership boundaries. Unchanged context, chosenAlternative, openQuestions, interactionWithShared and companion path must therefore be reconsidered with their changed dependencies. Fresh visual inspection must retry the outstanding rendering verification. All eight effective findings are carried for reassessment, with none resolved during preparation.","chunkMapping":[{"priorIds":["scope"],"currentIds":["scope"],"explanation":"Responsibility remains issue traceability and architectural choice. Upstream citations move from indices 7/8 to 8/9, and decision A adds index 10. Changed prompt exceptions require fresh assessment."},{"priorIds":["vault"],"currentIds":["vault"],"explanation":"Responsibility remains vault contracts, migration, errors and unit verification. Mutation ordering, per-name states, validation, recovery and tests changed; no coverage is retained."},{"priorIds":["runtime"],"currentIds":["runtime"],"explanation":"Responsibility remains lifecycle, consumers and ownership, now explicitly including the new global maintenance guard and citation 7. Changed exclusion and injection contracts require fresh review of unchanged entry points and dependencies."},{"priorIds":["visuals"],"currentIds":["visuals"],"explanation":"Responsibility remains sequence source and generated rendering. The document selector changes from line 191 to 208, sequence behavior changes, and prior rendering verification was incomplete."},{"priorIds":["consistency"],"currentIds":["consistency"],"explanation":"The final consistency responsibility and dependency topology are preserved, but the result must be freshly produced after all current substantive reviews."}],"retainedCoverage":[],"carriedFindingIds":["[1,\"scope\",\"scope-001\"]","[1,\"vault\",\"vault-001\"]","[1,\"vault\",\"vault-002\"]","[1,\"vault\",\"vault-003\"]","[1,\"vault\",\"vault-004\"]","[1,\"runtime\",\"runtime-001\"]","[1,\"runtime\",\"runtime-002\"]","[1,\"visuals\",\"visuals-001\"]"],"consistencyChunkIds":["consistency"]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"impact","phase":"impact","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"vault","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"runtime","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"visuals","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":2,"retriesUsed":1,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Resolution requires accepted fresh inspection without mandatory gaps"}],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1","attempt":2,"artifactId":"LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":4,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The LLD restores the originating issue’s full scope, preserves standalone ancestry, and carries forward applicable constraints from the prior LLD. Decision A records migration and save exceptions, but the claimed lifetime migration-prompt bound contradicts the specified retry behavior.","findings":[{"id":"scope-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/summary; /body/alternativesConsidered/0/cons","message":"The design promises that each legacy item prompts only once in its lifetime, but its failure behavior cannot preserve that bound. When a legacy read succeeds and its vault copy fails, the value is cached only for the current run and migration retries next run. If access was granted with Allow, that next legacy read can prompt again. A refused legacy read also retries after five minutes. Citation c11 records acceptance of a prompt when first copying each item, without addressing these repeated attempts, while openQuestions is empty. Qualify the lifetime claim to successful migration and explicitly reconcile retry prompts with the accepted exception, including corresponding acceptance coverage.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:11 — once-in-a-lifetime migration exception","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:236 — failed copy caches the value this run and retries next run","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:240 — refused legacy reads retry after five minutes","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:313 — repeats the lifetime prompt bound",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json — /citations/10 and /body/openQuestions","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md — Expected behavior and Fix intent 2"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:25","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/10","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261105669ae7a3/S001/LLD.md","src/shared/keystore.ts","src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts","src/daemon/index.ts:470","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts","node_modules/keytar/src/keytar_mac.cc"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"vault","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected all assigned vault selectors against the originating issue, canonical artifact and current consumers. Mutation serialization, migration caching, retirement and recovery losses are now specified. Runtime mutation validation remains a gap that can turn one malformed IPC save into an unreadable consolidated vault.","findings":[{"id":"vault-005","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/1; /body/dataModelChanges/0; /body/testStrategy","message":"The design validates the complete payload only on load, but does not require runtime validation of mutation arguments or the candidate payload before persistence. Current keys.set handlers merely cast unknown IPC params; keytar currently rejects non-string account/password arguments. Consolidation removes that protection because keytar receives fixed service/account strings and a serialized JSON string. For example, keys.set with {name:\"brave\",value:42} can persist a numeric secret under the specified write rules, then make the entire vault fail validation on restart, blocking unrelated credentials. Require runtime name/value validation at the vault owner boundary, or equivalent candidate-payload validation before every write, and test malformed IPC saves/deletes leave both memory and persisted content unchanged.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:58 — setKey specifies TypeScript arguments and persistence ordering without runtime input validation","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:141 — whole-payload validation occurs on load and rejects non-string secret values","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474 — keys.set casts params and passes name/value directly to setKey","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1488 — keys.delete likewise relies on a TypeScript cast","src/daemon/server.ts:95 — directDispatch passes request.params to the handler without method-specific validation","node_modules/keytar/src/main.cc:17 — existing native boundary rejects non-string usernames","node_modules/keytar/src/main.cc:25 — existing native boundary rejects non-string passwords",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json — /body/testStrategy/testLevels/0 covers malformed stored payloads, but not malformed mutation inputs"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/1","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261105669ae7a3/S001/LLD.md","src/shared/keystore.ts","src/daemon/db/secrets.ts","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474","src/daemon/server.ts","src/daemon/tools/config.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/notify/index.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/web/index.ts","src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts","node_modules/keytar/lib/keytar.js","node_modules/keytar/src/main.cc"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Add explicit listKeys compatibility tests for unmigrated, migrated, failed-copy-cached, retired and restored names; the current enumeration test checks only that findCredentials is not called.","Explicitly include duplicate retired names and overlapping secrets/retired membership in malformed-payload fixtures, matching the newly stated validation contract.","The current scope review already records the lifetime migration-prompt contradiction as scope-002. Apply its qualification consistently to migration step 3 and distinguish immediate repository-open retries from Keychain retries after the cooldown."]},{"chunkId":"runtime","status":"passed","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the originating ISSUE, applicable prior LLD and current runtime code. The proposed lifecycle, main-thread vault ownership, maintenance guard and below-vault test injection are feasible. No additional blocking defect was demonstrated within this assignment.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/citations/0","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261105669ae7a3/S001/LLD.md","src/shared/keystore.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts","src/shared/daemon-process.ts","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts","src/cli/services/connection-maintenance.ts","src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts","src/daemon/db/management-tickets.ts","src/daemon/db/management.ts","src/daemon/db/management-adoption.ts","src/daemon/db/secrets.ts","src/daemon/db/pool-cache.ts","src/daemon/db/__tests__/management-defaults.test.ts","src/daemon/connection-management-rpc.ts","src/daemon/connection-session-rpc.ts","src/daemon/db-rpc.ts","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474","src/daemon/index.ts:468","src/daemon/index.ts:596","src/daemon/server.ts:283","src/daemon/shutdown.ts","src/daemon/run-file-ownership.ts","src/daemon/threads/channel.ts","src/daemon/threads/main-services.ts:207","src/daemon/threads/worker-entry.ts:66","src/daemon/threads/session-worker.ts:57","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:73","src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts:368","src/daemon/tools/config.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/notify/index.ts:18","src/daemon/tools/builtins/web/index.ts:68","node_modules/keytar/src/async.cc"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Expand integration subjects to exercise owner, safeList, legacy listing and save independently; include threads-disabled operation, unrelated-request progress during a held read, repository isolation, concurrent maintenance admission and orphan-guard recovery. The current generic first-management-request subject could exercise capabilities alone.","Specify the hub operation payloads and forwarder error reconstruction explicitly. src/daemon/threads/channel.ts currently transports ordinary errors as name/message-only HubRemoteError instances and drops their cause; the forwarder should deliberately produce the promised KeystoreUnavailableError without worker-local fallback.","Clarify the retry test wording: an immediate request after denial retries the repository opener but receives the cached vault failure; Keychain access retries only after the five-minute cooldown.","Retain the prior LLD's explicit distinction between ticket-key, rollback-copy and connection-secret failures in integration assertions, including fixed client messages and unchanged recovery handling for missing secrets."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"Inspected the complete sequence definition, all four participants, and generated companion source. The companion preserves the authored messages and descriptions, but its legacy-path conditions conflict with the vault contracts. Actual rendering could not be verified.","findings":[{"id":"visuals-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/sequenceDefinition/messages/4-6","message":"The legacy branch is guarded only by the name being absent from the vault. This also includes retired names and names with cached legacy results, for which the contracts prohibit another legacy lookup. The following copy message additionally lacks the condition that a legacy value was found, although the preceding return explicitly permits no value. The generated companion repeats these conditions. Specify that fallback requires a non-retired name without a reusable run result, and that persistence requires a found value plus the mutation-queue recheck. Otherwise the sequence directs unnecessary Keychain access for deleted or cached names and a write for an absent name, contradicting the deletion and no-write guarantees.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition/messages/4, /5 and /6","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded Mermaid steps 5–7 and corresponding Messages descriptions","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:161 — cached, absent and retired-name rules","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:258 — absent lookup causes no write","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:261 — retired names must not fall back"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/companions","document:line:208","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts","src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts","src/shared/keystore.ts"],"limitations":["Mandatory rendered inspection of /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html could not be completed: opening the companion through the browser tool returned 'The browser access host is unavailable'. Source and retained descriptions were inspected; layout, readability and successful diagram rendering remain unverified."],"advice":["Consider extending the sequence with the main-thread on-demand management-opening path and annotating the mutually exclusive offline maintenance owner. Those boundaries are described in the surrounding contracts but are outside this diagram's stated secret-read scope.","Clarify the Keychain participant description: legacy items remain after successful copying until explicitly deleted, rather than existing only 'until copied'."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"Reconciled the current LLD, originating ISSUE, applicable prior design, canonical content, generated companion source and all four accepted substantive reviews. Six prior findings are resolved by freshly inspected contracts; the scope finding is superseded by the current prompt-bound finding. The prior visual finding remains carried because fresh visual inspection has a mandatory rendering gap. Current substantive findings require changes; unavailable rendered verification makes the overall consistency result incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261105669ae7a3/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html","src/shared/keystore.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474","src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts","node_modules/keytar/src/main.cc"],"limitations":["Mandatory rendered verification of /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html remains incomplete. The accepted fresh visuals chunk reports that browser access failed with 'The browser access host is unavailable'. This consistency inspection verified the embedded Mermaid and description tables, which cannot establish successful rendering, layout or readability. Consequently, visuals-001 cannot be resolved or superseded using the incomplete fresh visual inspection."],"advice":["Retain current findings scope-002, vault-005 and visuals-002 without duplicating them here. They respectively cover contradictory migration prompt bounds, malformed mutation inputs capable of corrupting the consolidated vault, and legacy sequence conditions inconsistent with retirement and cached-result contracts.","Apply scope-002 consistently to the summary, alternative a1, migration step 3, sequence narrative and generated message descriptions. Distinguish successful migration from failed-copy retries on later runs and refused-read retries after five minutes.","The repository opener's immediate retry and the keystore's five-minute cooldown can coexist: an immediate request retries opening but receives the cached keystore failure. Make this distinction explicit in the integration subject and acceptance mapping.","Preserve the runtime review's optional coverage recommendations for individual management entry points, unrelated-request progress, repository isolation and guard recovery. Preserve the vault review's enumeration and malformed-payload fixture recommendations.","The prior narrowed LLD supplies applicable lifecycle and error-handling constraints, but its earlier scope split does not limit this full-scope replacement. Decision A now records the migration and save exceptions; scope-002 identifies the remaining inconsistency in their stated bound."],"findingDecisions":[{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-001"},"rationale":"Fresh scope inspection confirms that citation c11 and the summary now explicitly capture stakeholder decision A accepting legacy migration and save prompts. This addresses the original absence of an authorized exception. The remaining inaccurate lifetime bound is assessed by the real current replacement scope-002.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: /citations/10 and /body/summary","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:11",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks scope, scope-002; limitations empty"],"action":"superseded","reviewedInChunkIds":["scope"],"supersededBy":{"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-002"}},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-001"},"rationale":"The current design puts migration copies, saves and deletes in one mutation queue, requires a fresh vault/retirement check before copying, and specifies per-name single-flight reads. Its test strategy now includes concurrent misses and migration interleavings with saves and deletes. Fresh vault inspection has no mandatory gaps.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:152","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:161","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-002"},"rationale":"Per-name run state now distinguishes in-flight lookup, copied value, cached value after failed persistence, absence and failed read with cooldown. Successful mutations clear the state. Repeated failed-copy reads and refused legacy-read cooldowns have explicit test subjects. This resolves the missing subsequent-read behavior.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:161","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:236","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-003"},"rationale":"Load validation now requires version 1, string-valued secrets, unique string retirement entries and disjoint membership. Map storage handles arbitrary account names, and malformed stored payloads have fail-closed test subjects. The current vault-005 concerns a distinct mutation-input boundary and does not invalidate resolution of this stored-payload validation defect.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:141","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:220","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-004"},"rationale":"Migration now explicitly describes abandonment as data-losing recovery, including loss of new secrets, reversion of changed legacy values and resurrection after failed legacy deletion. Steps 3 and 4 are marked non-rollbackable, with the mutation boundary caveat stated. Fresh vault inspection confirms the misleading recovery claims are corrected.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:187","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:313","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:314",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"runtime","findingId":"runtime-001"},"rationale":"The maintenance process now acquires the global guard before checking daemon control files and holds it through exit. Daemon vault loading occurs after socket publication and checks for that guard first. This ordering excludes simultaneous snapshots; atomic guard acquisition also excludes concurrent maintenance owners. Conflict, release and crash behavior are specified, with integration subjects. Fresh runtime inspection finds the protocol feasible without mandatory gaps.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:178","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:224","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:286","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts: acquireRunFileGuard and runFileGuardConflict",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks runtime"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["runtime"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"runtime","findingId":"runtime-002"},"rationale":"The test design replaces the above-vault database-port fixture with backend injection below the vault. A node --import preload installs it in spawned daemon and maintenance processes and rejects backend calls from workers. This exercises shared consumers and owner routing instead of bypassing the implementation. Fresh runtime inspection accepts its feasibility.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:282","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:285","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:287",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks runtime"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["runtime"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-001"},"rationale":"Current source qualifies the copied-name path and adds legacy messages, but the accepted fresh visuals inspection remains incomplete because rendering was unavailable. It also identifies incorrect legacy conditions as visuals-002. Preserve the prior origin unresolved rather than treating source revision intent or an inspection with mandatory gaps as sufficient resolution or supersession.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded Mermaid and Messages table",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks visuals, visuals-002 and rendering limitation"],"action":"carry"}]}],"limitations":["Mandatory rendered inspection of /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html could not be completed: opening the companion through the browser tool returned 'The browser access host is unavailable'. Source and retained descriptions were inspected; layout, readability and successful diagram rendering remain unverified.","Mandatory rendered verification of /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html remains incomplete. The accepted fresh visuals chunk reports that browser access failed with 'The browser access host is unavailable'. This consistency inspection verified the embedded Mermaid and description tables, which cannot establish successful rendering, layout or readability. Consequently, visuals-001 cannot be resolved or superseded using the incomplete fresh visual inspection."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"b9052f1142ff87b95aa661456e9b82210feb23ad1a54a9938abd7c82a54c7581","impact":{"baselineAttempt":1,"mode":"full","coverageOrigins":[{"chunkId":"scope","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"vault","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"runtime","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"visuals","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"consistency","kind":"fresh"}],"findingDecisions":[{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-001"},"rationale":"Fresh scope inspection confirms that citation c11 and the summary now explicitly capture stakeholder decision A accepting legacy migration and save prompts. This addresses the original absence of an authorized exception. The remaining inaccurate lifetime bound is assessed by the real current replacement scope-002.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: /citations/10 and /body/summary","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:11",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks scope, scope-002; limitations empty"],"action":"superseded","reviewedInChunkIds":["scope"],"supersededBy":{"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-002"}},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-001"},"rationale":"The current design puts migration copies, saves and deletes in one mutation queue, requires a fresh vault/retirement check before copying, and specifies per-name single-flight reads. Its test strategy now includes concurrent misses and migration interleavings with saves and deletes. Fresh vault inspection has no mandatory gaps.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:152","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:161","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-002"},"rationale":"Per-name run state now distinguishes in-flight lookup, copied value, cached value after failed persistence, absence and failed read with cooldown. Successful mutations clear the state. Repeated failed-copy reads and refused legacy-read cooldowns have explicit test subjects. This resolves the missing subsequent-read behavior.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:161","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:236","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-003"},"rationale":"Load validation now requires version 1, string-valued secrets, unique string retirement entries and disjoint membership. Map storage handles arbitrary account names, and malformed stored payloads have fail-closed test subjects. The current vault-005 concerns a distinct mutation-input boundary and does not invalidate resolution of this stored-payload validation defect.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:141","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:220","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:283",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-004"},"rationale":"Migration now explicitly describes abandonment as data-losing recovery, including loss of new secrets, reversion of changed legacy values and resurrection after failed legacy deletion. Steps 3 and 4 are marked non-rollbackable, with the mutation boundary caveat stated. Fresh vault inspection confirms the misleading recovery claims are corrected.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:187","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:313","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:314",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks vault"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["vault"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"runtime","findingId":"runtime-001"},"rationale":"The maintenance process now acquires the global guard before checking daemon control files and holds it through exit. Daemon vault loading occurs after socket publication and checks for that guard first. This ordering excludes simultaneous snapshots; atomic guard acquisition also excludes concurrent maintenance owners. Conflict, release and crash behavior are specified, with integration subjects. Fresh runtime inspection finds the protocol feasible without mandatory gaps.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:178","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:224","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:286","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts: acquireRunFileGuard and runFileGuardConflict",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks runtime"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["runtime"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"runtime","findingId":"runtime-002"},"rationale":"The test design replaces the above-vault database-port fixture with backend injection below the vault. A node --import preload installs it in spawned daemon and maintenance processes and rejects backend calls from workers. This exercises shared consumers and owner routing instead of bypassing the implementation. Fresh runtime inspection accepts its feasibility.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:282","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:285","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:287",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks runtime"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["runtime"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-001"},"rationale":"Current source qualifies the copied-name path and adds legacy messages, but the accepted fresh visuals inspection remains incomplete because rendering was unavailable. It also identifies incorrect legacy conditions as visuals-002. Preserve the prior origin unresolved rather than treating source revision intent or an inspection with mandatory gaps as sufficient resolution or supersession.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded Mermaid and Messages table",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: attempt 2 completedChunks visuals, visuals-002 and rendering limitation"],"action":"carry"}],"effectiveFindingOrigins":[{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-001"},{"attempt":2,"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-002"},{"attempt":2,"chunkId":"vault","findingId":"vault-005"},{"attempt":2,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-002"}]}},"finishedAt":"2026-11-08T12:55:35.353Z"},{"number":3,"status":"incomplete","preparationKind":"impact","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"62ddc27d0ea7fc1e4b3b8067763f83d88ce87c726d12629ff86a3fc6d432e4ab","document":"e426c628ba653a462d577e95f997390b3ec0bc99b10686095b4adf539953754d"},"contentIdentity":"7d64cdc03c4ad23f7ea5b10df9e029b5ba6c44e943433e93fdd50847fd9d222f","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"design.story\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1794155046486-rhpg48\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-08T16:27:24.990Z\",\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-11-04T19:31:14.890Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"cli-claude\",\n          \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 198089,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"fefa97b991537da7\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"open-saved-connections-demand-read-all\",\n    \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n    \"hldBaseRunId\": \"wf-1794155046486-rhpg48\",\n    \"hldEffectiveHash\": \"675d6e30fa2d8cdec33594860b5e18044827435d94375c35c958226946de86de\",\n    \"hldAmendmentsApplied\": [],\n    \"storyTitle\": \"Open saved connections on demand and read all credentials with one keychain prompt per daemon run\",\n    \"standalone\": true,\n    \"sizeClass\": \"bugfix\",\n    \"triageRationale\": \"Sized bugfix ISSUE-fefa97b991537da7; rerun at the issue's full scope on the user's instruction, revised after design review round 2 with stakeholder decision A.\",\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"envelope\": {\n      \"attachments\": []\n    },\n    \"revision\": 3\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"audience\": \"technical\",\n      \"prose\": \"The daemon stops touching the Keychain when it starts, and opens a repository's saved connections the first time a request needs them. All secrets move into one Keychain item that the main thread reads once per daemon run and serves to every thread from memory. By stakeholder decision A (2026-11-08) these exceptions to one prompt are accepted: each existing per-item secret prompts when it is successfully copied across, because macOS guards each old item separately; a failed copy or a denied dialog can prompt again on a later attempt; and a save may show one more dialog if the first was answered Allow rather than Always Allow.\"\n    },\n    \"hldContextSlice\": {\n      \"frameworkSummary\": \"Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\",\n      \"ownedContracts\": [],\n      \"consumedContracts\": [],\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n        \"owns\": [],\n        \"depends\": [],\n        \"internal\": \"Open saved connections on demand and read all credentials with one keychain prompt per daemon run\"\n      },\n      \"adjacentBoundaries\": [],\n      \"rolloutPhase\": \"standalone\",\n      \"nonFunctional\": {}\n    },\n    \"contractDetails\": {\n      \"surfaceLevel\": \"internal\",\n      \"api\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"getKey\",\n          \"signature\": \"getKey(name: string): Promise<string | null>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"name\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Secret name, unchanged from today's account names.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<string | null>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"The secret from the vault held in memory or from this run's cached legacy value, or null when no such secret exists.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"KeystoreInputError\",\n              \"condition\": \"The name is not a non-empty string. Nothing is read.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"KeystoreUnavailableError\",\n              \"condition\": \"The vault could not be loaded or validated, the offline maintenance tool holds the vault guard, or this name's legacy read failed. The cause is carried. Other requests are not blocked.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"On a session worker the call is forwarded over the worker's hub channel; only the owning thread calls keytar.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"At most one Keychain read of the vault item per successful daemon run, across all threads and concurrent callers.\",\n            \"A name absent from the vault, not retired and with no reusable run result has at most one legacy lookup in flight, and at most one successful legacy read per run.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"setKey\",\n          \"signature\": \"setKey(name: string, value: string): Promise<void>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"name\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Secret name.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"value\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Secret value.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<void>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Resolves after the vault item is written and memory updated.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"KeystoreInputError\",\n              \"condition\": \"The name is not a non-empty string or the value is not a string, checked at runtime at the vault owner because IPC params are only cast. Nothing is written and memory is unchanged.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"KeystoreUnavailableError\",\n              \"condition\": \"The vault could not be loaded or written. Memory keeps its previous value.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Runs in the owner's single mutation queue.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"The candidate payload passes the same validation as a load before it is written, so a write can never produce an item that later fails to load.\",\n            \"The Keychain item is written first; memory changes only after that succeeds.\",\n            \"Any run state held for the name is cleared and the name leaves the retired list.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"deleteKey\",\n          \"signature\": \"deleteKey(name: string): Promise<void>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"name\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Secret name.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<void>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Resolves after the name is removed from the vault and recorded as retired.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"KeystoreInputError\",\n              \"condition\": \"The name is not a non-empty string. Nothing is written and memory is unchanged.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"KeystoreUnavailableError\",\n              \"condition\": \"The vault could not be loaded or written. Memory is unchanged.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Runs in the owner's single mutation queue.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"The name is recorded as retired, so a leftover legacy item or an in-flight copy cannot bring it back.\",\n            \"The legacy item is deleted best effort; a failure is logged by name only.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"listKeys\",\n          \"signature\": \"listKeys(): Promise<string[]>\",\n          \"parameters\": [],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<string[]>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Names held in the vault. A legacy item not yet copied in is not listed until it is first used or set.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"KeystoreUnavailableError\",\n              \"condition\": \"The vault could not be loaded.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"keytar.findCredentials is no longer called anywhere.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"ensureDefaultManagedRoot\",\n          \"signature\": \"ensureDefaultManagedRoot(root: string, ports?: StartupPorts): Promise<void>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"root\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Registered repository whose saved management a request needs.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"ports\",\n              \"type\": \"StartupPorts\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Unchanged registration, keystore and enablement seams.\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<void>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Unchanged: resolves once saved management for the root is installed, memoised per root; a rejected attempt is forgotten so the next call retries. What changes is the caller: the boot loop is removed and the main-thread request handlers call it.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"TicketError('secret-unavailable')\",\n              \"condition\": \"The Keychain refused or failed reading or creating the root's ticket key.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"ManagedStoreError('recovery-required') with cause KeystoreUnavailableError\",\n              \"condition\": \"A rollback-copy or connection-secret read failed in the Keychain; managementRejection reports it as 'secret-unavailable' from the cause.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"ManagedStoreError('recovery-required')\",\n              \"condition\": \"A legacy unmanaged registry, damaged metadata or any other integrity failure; unchanged.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Called on the daemon main thread only, by owner and safeList and the listing and save paths, as capabilities already does.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"No call is made before server.listen, so a daemon start reads nothing from the Keychain.\",\n            \"Fresh initialization takes its ticket key before its first disk write, so a refused Keychain read leaves no partial state.\",\n            \"closeDefaultManagedRoots still closes every root opened on demand at shutdown.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dataModelChanges\": [\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"SecretVaultItem\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"One Keychain item under the new service 'insrc-vault', reserved account 'secrets', with a value of JSON: version 1, secrets (a map of name to value) and retired (names deleted after the vault existed). The separate service means keys.get, keys.set, keys.delete and keys.list can never address the vault item itself. The whole payload is validated on load and before every write: an object with version exactly 1, secrets an object whose values are all strings, retired an array of unique strings, and no name in both. Entries are held in a Map, so an arbitrary account name such as __proto__ is an ordinary key. A validation failure on load is fail-closed: the item is never overwritten and reads report KeystoreUnavailableError.\",\n        \"schemaDiff\": \"+ service insrc-vault, account secrets: { version: 1, secrets: Record<string, string>, retired: string[] }\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/shared/keystore.ts:10-40\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"In-memory vault\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"Owned by the main thread, or by the offline maintenance process. Names and values are checked at runtime at this boundary, on every thread's request, because the keys handlers only cast their IPC params. Load is single-flight, so a pending dialog holds one load and concurrent callers await it. A refused or failed load is remembered for five minutes, in which reads fail at once with KeystoreUnavailableError, so a user who denies access is not prompted by every following request. Every change to the vault, including a migration copy, runs in one mutation queue that writes the Keychain item first and memory only after success. Decrypted values stay in memory and pass between threads only over the in-process hub channel; nothing decrypted is written to disk or logged.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/shared/keystore.ts:10-40\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/main-services.ts:207\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/worker-entry.ts:81\",\n          \"src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474-1503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Per-name run state\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"In memory for the run only, for a name absent from the vault and not retired. Lookup in flight: one legacy read per name, shared by concurrent callers. Copied: the found value entered the vault and the state is dropped; this is the successful copy after which the name never reads its legacy item again. Cached value: the read succeeded but the copy failed, so this run's later reads are served from memory with no further Keychain access and the copy is retried on the next run, where the legacy read can prompt again. Absent: the legacy item does not exist, so null is returned for the rest of the run with no write. Failed: the legacy read was refused, so reads of that name fail at once for five minutes and then retry, which can prompt again. Both retries are accepted exceptions under decision A. A setKey or deleteKey clears the name's state. A copy happens only for a found value and commits inside the mutation queue only if the name is still neither in the vault nor retired, so a copy that lost a race with a save or delete is discarded.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/shared/keystore.ts:10-40\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Worker keystore forwarding\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"A hub operation served by the main thread through serveHub for get, set, delete and list; worker-entry installs the forwarder, so getKey and its siblings keep their signatures on every thread. With daemon.threads.enabled off, the main thread uses the vault directly. No RPC method is added, so the method-class table is unchanged.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/daemon/threads/channel.ts:117\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/main-services.ts:207\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/worker-entry.ts:81\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts:142-160\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Vault run-file guard\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"A guard directory under ~/.insrc, created with acquireRunFileGuard. The offline maintenance binary acquires it first, then performs its existing pid and socket absence check, and holds it until exit. A daemon checks runFileGuardConflict before loading the vault and fails with KeystoreUnavailableError while it is held, without touching the Keychain and without the five-minute memory. The ordering closes the race: a daemon only loads the vault after its socket is open, so a maintenance run that acquires the guard either sees that socket and refuses, or holds the guard before the daemon's first load. A maintenance crash leaves the guard in place, fail-closed, and the error names its path for an operator to clear, as run-file guards already do.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts:14-24\",\n          \"src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts:52\",\n          \"src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts:64\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Legacy per-item secrets\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"Items under service 'insrc' stop being the source of truth once copied, and migration never deletes them, so a failed or partial migration leaves them readable. Only an explicit deleteKey removes one. Abandoning the vault is a recovery that loses data: see the migration section.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/shared/keystore.ts:10-40\",\n          \"src/daemon/db/secrets.ts:26-44\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"keys.list handler\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"Today it runs one Keychain read per name; it now reads names and values through the vault. No in-repo client calls keys.list today.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474-1503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Daemon boot\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"Today the daemon opens every registered repository before server.listen; that loop is removed, and closeDefaultManagedRoots stays registered for shutdown.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/daemon/index.ts:470-476\",\n          \"src/daemon/index.ts:539\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"interactionWithShared\": [],\n    \"errorPaths\": {\n      \"errorCases\": [\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A save, delete or read arrives with a malformed name or value\",\n          \"detection\": \"The runtime type check at the vault owner boundary fails\",\n          \"response\": \"KeystoreInputError; the mutation queue is not entered and neither memory nor the Keychain changes.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"That request fails; other secrets stay readable.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The user denies the Keychain dialog, or the Keychain read of the vault item fails\",\n          \"detection\": \"keytar.getPassword rejects during the single-flight vault load\",\n          \"response\": \"Every waiting caller gets KeystoreUnavailableError with the cause. The failure is remembered for five minutes, in which reads fail at once without a dialog; the next read after that retries.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"Requests needing a secret report the connection unavailable with the cause; requests needing no secret continue.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The vault item fails validation on load\",\n          \"detection\": \"JSON parsing, the version check or the whole-payload shape check fails after a successful Keychain read\",\n          \"response\": \"Fail closed: KeystoreUnavailableError, the item is never rewritten and no legacy fallback is used, so a damaged item cannot be replaced by a partial one.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"Saved secrets are unavailable until the item is repaired or deliberately abandoned.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A candidate payload fails validation before a write\",\n          \"detection\": \"The same whole-payload check runs on the candidate inside the mutation queue\",\n          \"response\": \"KeystoreUnavailableError; nothing is written and memory is unchanged.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The save fails and the existing vault stays readable.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The offline maintenance tool holds the vault guard when a daemon needs a secret\",\n          \"detection\": \"runFileGuardConflict reports the guard before the vault load\",\n          \"response\": \"KeystoreUnavailableError naming the guard, with no Keychain access and no five-minute memory, so the first request after the guard is released succeeds.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"Requests needing a secret fail until maintenance ends; a crashed maintenance run leaves the guard for an operator to clear.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The maintenance tool finds the daemon running after taking the guard\",\n          \"detection\": \"The existing pid and socket absence check, now made after the guard is acquired, finds a file\",\n          \"response\": \"The tool releases the guard and exits with its existing failure message, without touching the vault.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"Maintenance does not run; management stays disabled pending recovery as today.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"Writing the vault item fails on a save or delete\",\n          \"detection\": \"keytar.setPassword rejects inside the mutation queue\",\n          \"response\": \"KeystoreUnavailableError to that caller; memory keeps its previous value, so memory and Keychain stay consistent.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The save reports failure and the old value remains in force.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"Copying a legacy secret into the vault fails\",\n          \"detection\": \"keytar.setPassword rejects inside the mutation queue after the legacy read found a value\",\n          \"response\": \"The value is kept as this run's cached value for the name and returned; the legacy item is untouched and the copy is retried on the next run.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"None this run; that name's legacy read on the next run can prompt again, an accepted exception under decision A.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A legacy item read is refused during migration\",\n          \"detection\": \"keytar.getPassword on the legacy service rejects\",\n          \"response\": \"KeystoreUnavailableError for that name only, remembered for five minutes per name; the vault and other names are unaffected.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"That connection is reported unavailable with the cause and is not re-prompted by each following request; the retry after five minutes can prompt again, an accepted exception under decision A.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"Opening a repository's saved connections fails on first use\",\n          \"detection\": \"ensureDefaultManagedRoot rejects with a keystore cause or an integrity failure\",\n          \"response\": \"The rejected attempt is forgotten, the request gets 'secret-unavailable' for a keystore cause and 'recovery-required' otherwise; fresh initialization has written nothing if its ticket key could not be taken.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"That repository's request fails with its cause; the daemon and other repositories are unaffected.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A worker's hub call to the vault owner fails or the channel closes\",\n          \"detection\": \"The hub request rejects on the worker\",\n          \"response\": \"KeystoreUnavailableError with the cause; the worker does not fall back to calling keytar itself.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"That request fails; no extra Keychain access occurs.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"edgeCases\": [\n        {\n          \"input\": \"No vault item exists yet\",\n          \"expected\": \"keytar returns null with no dialog for a missing item; the vault starts empty and the item is created on the first write.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A name exists nowhere, such as an unset web search key\",\n          \"expected\": \"getKey returns null; the absence is remembered for the run, not persisted, so a lookup causes no write.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A save or delete lands while a legacy read for the same name is in flight\",\n          \"expected\": \"The save or delete wins; the copy finds the name in the vault or retired inside the mutation queue and is discarded.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Two callers miss the same name at once\",\n          \"expected\": \"They share one legacy read and one copy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A name is deleted and an old legacy item for it remains\",\n          \"expected\": \"The retired list stops the legacy fallback, and getKey returns null with no legacy read.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A retired name is saved again\",\n          \"expected\": \"setKey adds it to secrets and removes it from retired.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An account name such as __proto__ or constructor\",\n          \"expected\": \"It is an ordinary key, because entries are held in a Map.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An empty string as a secret value\",\n          \"expected\": \"It is a valid string and is stored; only a non-string value is refused.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Many threads ask for different secrets while the first dialog is open\",\n          \"expected\": \"They wait on the one load; exactly one Keychain read of the vault occurs and requests needing no secret do not wait.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"daemon.threads.enabled is false\",\n          \"expected\": \"The main thread uses the vault directly with the same behaviour.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A plain listing of a repository with no management marker\",\n          \"expected\": \"No state is created and the Keychain is not touched.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"invariantsToPreserve\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"getKey, setKey, deleteKey and listKeys keep their signatures, and the KeystoreLike port and its test seam keep working.\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"ensureDefaultManagedRoot stays memoised per root and forgets a failed attempt.\",\n          \"source\": \"c3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The CLI never opens the Keychain; only daemon code and the daemon-owned offline maintenance binary do.\",\n          \"source\": \"c4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Hub traffic stays in-process between the main thread and its workers.\",\n          \"source\": \"c5\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"A daemon shutdown still closes every root that was opened.\",\n          \"source\": \"c3\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"testStrategy\": {\n      \"testFramework\": \"node:test\",\n      \"testLevels\": [\n        {\n          \"level\": \"unit\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The vault's load, read, write, retire, validation, ordering and failure rules against a fake Keychain backend injected below the vault that counts calls.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"vault: concurrent reads perform one Keychain read\",\n            \"vault: a refused load fails at once for five minutes and then retries\",\n            \"vault: a payload with a bad version, missing secrets, a non-string value or a bad retired list fails closed and is never rewritten\",\n            \"vault: a malformed name or value leaves memory and the stored item unchanged\",\n            \"vault: a name such as __proto__ is stored and read as an ordinary key\",\n            \"vault: a failed write leaves memory unchanged\",\n            \"vault: concurrent saves lose no update\",\n            \"vault: a retired name does not fall back to its legacy item\",\n            \"vault: a retired name saved again is readable\",\n            \"migration: a legacy secret is copied once and read from the vault afterwards\",\n            \"migration: concurrent misses of one name share one legacy read and one copy\",\n            \"migration: a save during a legacy read wins and the copy is discarded\",\n            \"migration: a delete during a legacy read wins and the copy is discarded\",\n            \"migration: a failed copy serves later reads from memory, keeps the legacy item and reads it again on the next run\",\n            \"migration: an absent name causes no write and no second lookup in the run\",\n            \"migration: a refused legacy read fails at once for five minutes for that name only and then retries\",\n            \"keystore: listKeys never calls findCredentials\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"A fake Keychain backend that counts reads and writes, can refuse them and can hold a read open, installed through a test-only setter below the vault\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"integration\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Thread ownership, process exclusion, on-demand opening and error mapping in real processes, with the fake backend installed below the vault in the process that owns it.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"threads: workers on two threads share one Keychain read\",\n            \"threads: a worker never calls the backend directly\",\n            \"threads: a closed hub channel does not fall back to the Keychain\",\n            \"threads: a save on one worker is visible on another\",\n            \"ipc: keys.set with a non-string value is refused and other secrets stay readable after a restart\",\n            \"guard: a daemon holding no vault fails requests while maintenance holds the guard and succeeds after release\",\n            \"guard: maintenance refuses and releases the guard when the daemon socket exists after acquiring it\",\n            \"boot: a daemon start reads nothing from the Keychain and opens its socket\",\n            \"on-demand: the first management request opens the repository and a later one does not reopen it\",\n            \"on-demand: a refused Keychain read reports secret-unavailable and the next request retries\",\n            \"on-demand: a refused first-time set-up leaves nothing on disk\",\n            \"on-demand: a plain listing of an unmanaged repository touches nothing\",\n            \"consumers: notify, web and keys handlers read through the vault\",\n            \"maintenance: the offline tool reads the vault once\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"A node --import test preload that installs the fake backend in a spawned daemon or maintenance process, so no production switch is added, and that throws if the backend is called on a worker\",\n            \"A temporary repository with seeded saved connections\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"live\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The real macOS behaviour no fake can show, run by a person.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"live: after a node upgrade one dialog appears across several connections and threads once migration is complete\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"A macOS login Keychain with several saved connections\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceMapping\": [\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac1\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"boot: a daemon start reads nothing from the Keychain and opens its socket\",\n            \"on-demand: the first management request opens the repository and a later one does not reopen it\",\n            \"on-demand: a refused Keychain read reports secret-unavailable and the next request retries\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac2\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"vault: concurrent reads perform one Keychain read\",\n            \"threads: workers on two threads share one Keychain read\",\n            \"threads: a save on one worker is visible on another\",\n            \"migration: a failed copy serves later reads from memory, keeps the legacy item and reads it again on the next run\",\n            \"migration: a refused legacy read fails at once for five minutes for that name only and then retries\",\n            \"live: after a node upgrade one dialog appears across several connections and threads once migration is complete\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac3\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"consumers: notify, web and keys handlers read through the vault\",\n            \"maintenance: the offline tool reads the vault once\",\n            \"guard: a daemon holding no vault fails requests while maintenance holds the guard and succeeds after release\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac4\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"migration: a legacy secret is copied once and read from the vault afterwards\",\n            \"migration: a save during a legacy read wins and the copy is discarded\",\n            \"migration: a delete during a legacy read wins and the copy is discarded\",\n            \"vault: a malformed name or value leaves memory and the stored item unchanged\",\n            \"ipc: keys.set with a non-string value is refused and other secrets stay readable after a restart\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"migration\": {\n      \"stateBefore\": \"Each secret is its own Keychain item under service 'insrc', read through keytar on every use (s1 symbol.locate), and main() opens every repository's saved connections before server.listen (s1 usage.example).\",\n      \"stateAfter\": \"One vault item under service 'insrc-vault' holds every secret and is read once per daemon run by the main thread; saved connections open on first use. Legacy items remain until an explicit delete.\",\n      \"migrationSteps\": [\n        {\n          \"order\": 1,\n          \"action\": \"Ship the vault with the legacy fallback: a name absent from the vault, not retired and with no reusable run result is read from its legacy item and, when a value is found, copied in on first use.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 2,\n          \"action\": \"Remove the boot loop and open saved connections on first request.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 3,\n          \"action\": \"Each legacy secret is copied into the vault the first time it is used; a successful copy shows at most one dialog for that item and that name never reads its legacy item again. A failed copy or a denied dialog can prompt again on a later attempt (accepted exceptions, stakeholder decision A). No legacy item is deleted by migration. Once any secret has been saved or deleted through the vault, going back loses data, as step 4 states.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 4,\n          \"action\": \"Recovery if the vault must be abandoned: delete the single vault item, or run the previous daemon version; both read the untouched legacy items. This is not a clean rollback. A secret first saved after migration is lost and must be re-entered; a secret changed after migration reverts to its older legacy value; a secret deleted after migration whose best-effort legacy delete failed comes back and must be deleted again.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": false\n        }\n      ],\n      \"backwardCompat\": \"getKey, setKey, deleteKey and listKeys keep their signatures and the KeystoreLike port and test seam are unchanged. A malformed name or value is now refused with KeystoreInputError where keytar refused it before. listKeys now reports vault names only, so a legacy item appears after first use; no in-repo client calls keys.list. A previous daemon version keeps reading legacy items and does not see the vault, with the losses stated in step 4.\",\n      \"zeroDowntime\": false,\n      \"dataRewriteRequired\": false\n    },\n    \"alternativesConsidered\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a1\",\n        \"name\": \"One Keychain item holding every secret, owned by the main thread\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"A JSON map of all secrets lives in one Keychain item under a new service; the main thread loads it once on first need and serves every thread from memory.\",\n        \"approach\": \"getKey, setKey, deleteKey and listKeys keep their signatures but use a vault: one Keychain item under a new service whose value is a versioned JSON map of name to secret. The first read loads it once, single-flight, and later reads come from memory. Workers forward over their existing hub channel, so only one thread touches the Keychain. The owner validates every name and value, and every change to the vault, including a migration copy, runs through one mutation queue that writes the item first and memory only after success. A name absent from the vault, not retired and with no reusable run result is read from its legacy item, single-flight per name, and a found value is copied in through that queue after re-checking the current state, so a stale copy cannot overwrite a save or undo a delete. Legacy items stay readable. The offline maintenance tool holds a cross-process guard for its whole run. The boot loop is removed and saved connections open on demand.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"The consolidated single item the issue asks for, chosen by the stakeholder as decision A\",\n          \"The Keychain stays the only place secrets rest\",\n          \"Existing callers keep their signatures\",\n          \"Reuses the worker hub channel and the run-file guard\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Accepted exception: a save rewrites the whole item, so macOS may show one more dialog when the first was answered Allow rather than Always Allow\",\n          \"Accepted exception: each legacy item prompts when it is successfully copied, and a failed copy or a denied dialog can prompt again on a later attempt, because macOS guards each legacy item separately\",\n          \"Workers gain a hub round trip for every secret read\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a2\",\n        \"name\": \"One Keychain master key with secrets in an encrypted file\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"The Keychain holds only an AES key; secrets live in an AES-GCM file under ~/.insrc, so saving a secret never touches the Keychain after the first read.\",\n        \"approach\": \"The vault keeps the same read and write surface and the same main-thread ownership, but its single Keychain item holds a random 256-bit key. Secrets are stored in one AES-GCM encrypted file written atomically under ~/.insrc; the key is read once per run and writes only re-encrypt the file. Migration and on-demand opening are as in a1.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Saving or removing a secret can never prompt once the key is in memory\",\n          \"Item size stays constant however many secrets are saved\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Introduces a new encrypted store with its own file format, integrity, atomic-write and permission rules\",\n          \"Secrets become recoverable only with both the file and the key, and daemon.backup would need to cover the file\",\n          \"Moves secrets out of the Keychain, and legacy items still prompt when migrated\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Removes the save dialog but moves secrets to a new encrypted store, and is only partial on lossless migration; the stakeholder declined it in decision A.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a3\",\n        \"name\": \"One Keychain item cached separately on each thread\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"The smallest change: the keystore module caches the single item in module scope, so each thread that needs a secret loads it for itself.\",\n        \"approach\": \"The keystore module holds the consolidated map in a module-level variable with no cross-thread forwarding. The main thread and each session worker load the item on their own first read and keep their own copy. Writes go to the Keychain and update only the writing thread's copy.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"No hub operations or worker forwarding\",\n          \"Smallest amount of code\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Every session worker repeats the Keychain access, so a user who answers Allow is prompted once per thread, which fails the one-prompt requirement\",\n          \"A write on one thread leaves stale secrets on every other thread\",\n          \"Two threads writing at once can lose an update to the shared item\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"S\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Violates the one-prompt requirement: each thread does its own Keychain access and holds a stale copy after a write.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"chosenAlternative\": \"a1\",\n    \"openQuestions\": [],\n    \"sequenceDefinition\": {\n      \"narrative\": \"How a secret read reaches the Keychain. The normal path, once a name is in the vault, needs only the one vault read per run. The migration path applies only to a name not in the vault, not retired and with no reusable run result, and is the prompt accepted in stakeholder decision A.\",\n      \"participants\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"client\",\n          \"label\": \"Client request\",\n          \"description\": \"A request that needs a saved secret.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"worker\",\n          \"label\": \"Session worker\",\n          \"description\": \"The thread running that session; it never calls the Keychain.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"main\",\n          \"label\": \"Main thread vault\",\n          \"description\": \"The one in-memory owner of all secrets and of the mutation queue.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"keychain\",\n          \"label\": \"macOS Keychain\",\n          \"description\": \"Holds the single vault item and, until copied, the legacy per-item secrets.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"messages\": [\n        {\n          \"from\": \"client\",\n          \"to\": \"worker\",\n          \"label\": \"request needing a secret\",\n          \"description\": \"No Keychain access has happened since the daemon started.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"main\",\n          \"label\": \"getKey over the hub channel\",\n          \"description\": \"Forwarded in-process.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"main\",\n          \"to\": \"keychain\",\n          \"label\": \"first need this run: read vault item once\",\n          \"description\": \"Single-flight, so concurrent callers wait on this one read and see one dialog.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"keychain\",\n          \"to\": \"main\",\n          \"label\": \"every secret copied so far\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\",\n          \"description\": \"Held in memory until the daemon exits.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"main\",\n          \"to\": \"keychain\",\n          \"label\": \"only if the name is not in the vault, not retired and has no reusable run result: read its legacy item\",\n          \"description\": \"A retired name, a cached value and a remembered absence or refusal never reach this step. One read per name however many callers miss it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"keychain\",\n          \"to\": \"main\",\n          \"label\": \"legacy secret, or nothing when no such item exists\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\",\n          \"description\": \"Nothing found means no copy and no write; the absence is remembered for the run.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"main\",\n          \"to\": \"keychain\",\n          \"label\": \"only if a value was found and the queue re-check passes: write vault with the copy\",\n          \"description\": \"The queue re-check discards the copy if a save or delete of that name won the race. A save or delete takes this same queue.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"main\",\n          \"to\": \"worker\",\n          \"label\": \"secret\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\",\n          \"description\": \"Passed in-process only.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"main\",\n          \"label\": \"later getKey of a copied name, any thread\",\n          \"description\": \"Served from memory with no Keychain access.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"companions\": [\n      {\n        \"kind\": \"diagram-mermaid\",\n        \"relPath\": \"docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html\",\n        \"title\": \"Sequence diagram\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/shared/keystore.ts:10-40\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/db/secrets.ts:26-44\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts:14-30\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/threads/channel.ts:117\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/index.ts:470-476\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts:142-160\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts:64\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c9\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"ISSUE-fefa97b991537da7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c10\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"LLD-669ae7a31701e106-S001\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c11\",\n      \"kind\": \"stakeholder\",\n      \"ref\": \"Decision A, 2026-11-08\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"Keep one Keychain item holding everything; accept that each legacy item prompts when successfully copied, that a failed copy or a denied dialog can prompt again on a later attempt, and that a save may show one more dialog if the first was answered Allow rather than Always Allow.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","document":"<!-- insrc:artifact LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1 -->\n\n# LLD: STORY-fefa97b991537da7-s1 — Open saved connections on demand and read all credentials with one keychain prompt per daemon run\n\n## Summary\n\n**Epic:** `open-saved-connections-demand-read-all`\n**HLD base run:** `wf-1794155046486-rhpg48`\n**HLD effective hash:** `675d6e30fa2d...`\n\nThe daemon stops touching the Keychain when it starts, and opens a repository's saved connections the first time a request needs them. All secrets move into one Keychain item that the main thread reads once per daemon run and serves to every thread from memory. By stakeholder decision A (2026-11-08) these exceptions to one prompt are accepted: each existing per-item secret prompts when it is successfully copied across, because macOS guards each old item separately; a failed copy or a denied dialog can prompt again on a later attempt; and a save may show one more dialog if the first was answered Allow rather than Always Allow.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [HLD context](#1-hld-context)\n2. [Contract details](#2-contract-details)\n3. [Data model changes](#3-data-model-changes)\n4. [Diagrams](#4-diagrams)\n5. [Error paths](#5-error-paths)\n6. [Test strategy](#6-test-strategy)\n7. [Migration](#7-migration)\n8. [Alternatives considered](#8-alternatives-considered)\n9. [References](#9-references)\n\n## 1. HLD context\n\n**Framework:** Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\n**Rollout phase:** standalone\n\n## 2. Contract details\n\n**Surface level:** internal\n\n### 2.1 `getKey`\n\n```typescript\ngetKey(name: string): Promise<string | null>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `name: string` — Secret name, unchanged from today's account names.\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<string | null>` — The secret from the vault held in memory or from this run's cached legacy value, or null when no such secret exists.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `KeystoreInputError` when The name is not a non-empty string. Nothing is read.\n- `KeystoreUnavailableError` when The vault could not be loaded or validated, the offline maintenance tool holds the vault guard, or this name's legacy read failed. The cause is carried. Other requests are not blocked.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- On a session worker the call is forwarded over the worker's hub channel; only the owning thread calls keytar.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- At most one Keychain read of the vault item per successful daemon run, across all threads and concurrent callers.\n- A name absent from the vault, not retired and with no reusable run result has at most one legacy lookup in flight, and at most one successful legacy read per run.\n\n### 2.2 `setKey`\n\n```typescript\nsetKey(name: string, value: string): Promise<void>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `name: string` — Secret name.\n- `value: string` — Secret value.\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<void>` — Resolves after the vault item is written and memory updated.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `KeystoreInputError` when The name is not a non-empty string or the value is not a string, checked at runtime at the vault owner because IPC params are only cast. Nothing is written and memory is unchanged.\n- `KeystoreUnavailableError` when The vault could not be loaded or written. Memory keeps its previous value.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- Runs in the owner's single mutation queue.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The candidate payload passes the same validation as a load before it is written, so a write can never produce an item that later fails to load.\n- The Keychain item is written first; memory changes only after that succeeds.\n- Any run state held for the name is cleared and the name leaves the retired list.\n\n### 2.3 `deleteKey`\n\n```typescript\ndeleteKey(name: string): Promise<void>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `name: string` — Secret name.\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<void>` — Resolves after the name is removed from the vault and recorded as retired.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `KeystoreInputError` when The name is not a non-empty string. Nothing is written and memory is unchanged.\n- `KeystoreUnavailableError` when The vault could not be loaded or written. Memory is unchanged.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- Runs in the owner's single mutation queue.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The name is recorded as retired, so a leftover legacy item or an in-flight copy cannot bring it back.\n- The legacy item is deleted best effort; a failure is logged by name only.\n\n### 2.4 `listKeys`\n\n```typescript\nlistKeys(): Promise<string[]>\n```\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<string[]>` — Names held in the vault. A legacy item not yet copied in is not listed until it is first used or set.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `KeystoreUnavailableError` when The vault could not be loaded.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- keytar.findCredentials is no longer called anywhere.\n\n### 2.5 `ensureDefaultManagedRoot`\n\n```typescript\nensureDefaultManagedRoot(root: string, ports?: StartupPorts): Promise<void>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `root: string` — Registered repository whose saved management a request needs.\n- `ports: StartupPorts` _(optional)_ — Unchanged registration, keystore and enablement seams.\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<void>` — Unchanged: resolves once saved management for the root is installed, memoised per root; a rejected attempt is forgotten so the next call retries. What changes is the caller: the boot loop is removed and the main-thread request handlers call it.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `TicketError('secret-unavailable')` when The Keychain refused or failed reading or creating the root's ticket key.\n- `ManagedStoreError('recovery-required') with cause KeystoreUnavailableError` when A rollback-copy or connection-secret read failed in the Keychain; managementRejection reports it as 'secret-unavailable' from the cause.\n- `ManagedStoreError('recovery-required')` when A legacy unmanaged registry, damaged metadata or any other integrity failure; unchanged.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- Called on the daemon main thread only, by owner and safeList and the listing and save paths, as capabilities already does.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- No call is made before server.listen, so a daemon start reads nothing from the Keychain.\n- Fresh initialization takes its ticket key before its first disk write, so a refused Keychain read leaves no partial state.\n- closeDefaultManagedRoots still closes every root opened on demand at shutdown.\n\n## 3. Data model changes\n\n### 3.1 `SecretVaultItem` — new\n\nOne Keychain item under the new service 'insrc-vault', reserved account 'secrets', with a value of JSON: version 1, secrets (a map of name to value) and retired (names deleted after the vault existed). The separate service means keys.get, keys.set, keys.delete and keys.list can never address the vault item itself. The whole payload is validated on load and before every write: an object with version exactly 1, secrets an object whose values are all strings, retired an array of unique strings, and no name in both. Entries are held in a Map, so an arbitrary account name such as __proto__ is an ordinary key. A validation failure on load is fail-closed: the item is never overwritten and reads report KeystoreUnavailableError.\n\n```\n+ service insrc-vault, account secrets: { version: 1, secrets: Record<string, string>, retired: string[] }\n```\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/shared/keystore.ts:10-40`\n\n### 3.2 `In-memory vault` — new\n\nOwned by the main thread, or by the offline maintenance process. Names and values are checked at runtime at this boundary, on every thread's request, because the keys handlers only cast their IPC params. Load is single-flight, so a pending dialog holds one load and concurrent callers await it. A refused or failed load is remembered for five minutes, in which reads fail at once with KeystoreUnavailableError, so a user who denies access is not prompted by every following request. Every change to the vault, including a migration copy, runs in one mutation queue that writes the Keychain item first and memory only after success. Decrypted values stay in memory and pass between threads only over the in-process hub channel; nothing decrypted is written to disk or logged.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/shared/keystore.ts:10-40`\n- `src/daemon/threads/main-services.ts:207`\n- `src/daemon/threads/worker-entry.ts:81`\n- `src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474-1503`\n\n### 3.3 `Per-name run state` — new\n\nIn memory for the run only, for a name absent from the vault and not retired. Lookup in flight: one legacy read per name, shared by concurrent callers. Copied: the found value entered the vault and the state is dropped; this is the successful copy after which the name never reads its legacy item again. Cached value: the read succeeded but the copy failed, so this run's later reads are served from memory with no further Keychain access and the copy is retried on the next run, where the legacy read can prompt again. Absent: the legacy item does not exist, so null is returned for the rest of the run with no write. Failed: the legacy read was refused, so reads of that name fail at once for five minutes and then retry, which can prompt again. Both retries are accepted exceptions under decision A. A setKey or deleteKey clears the name's state. A copy happens only for a found value and commits inside the mutation queue only if the name is still neither in the vault nor retired, so a copy that lost a race with a save or delete is discarded.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/shared/keystore.ts:10-40`\n\n### 3.4 `Worker keystore forwarding` — new\n\nA hub operation served by the main thread through serveHub for get, set, delete and list; worker-entry installs the forwarder, so getKey and its siblings keep their signatures on every thread. With daemon.threads.enabled off, the main thread uses the vault directly. No RPC method is added, so the method-class table is unchanged.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/daemon/threads/channel.ts:117`\n- `src/daemon/threads/main-services.ts:207`\n- `src/daemon/threads/worker-entry.ts:81`\n- `src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts:142-160`\n\n### 3.5 `Vault run-file guard` — new\n\nA guard directory under ~/.insrc, created with acquireRunFileGuard. The offline maintenance binary acquires it first, then performs its existing pid and socket absence check, and holds it until exit. A daemon checks runFileGuardConflict before loading the vault and fails with KeystoreUnavailableError while it is held, without touching the Keychain and without the five-minute memory. The ordering closes the race: a daemon only loads the vault after its socket is open, so a maintenance run that acquires the guard either sees that socket and refuses, or holds the guard before the daemon's first load. A maintenance crash leaves the guard in place, fail-closed, and the error names its path for an operator to clear, as run-file guards already do.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts:14-24`\n- `src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts:52`\n- `src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts:64`\n\n### 3.6 `Legacy per-item secrets` — invariant-change\n\nItems under service 'insrc' stop being the source of truth once copied, and migration never deletes them, so a failed or partial migration leaves them readable. Only an explicit deleteKey removes one. Abandoning the vault is a recovery that loses data: see the migration section.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/shared/keystore.ts:10-40`\n- `src/daemon/db/secrets.ts:26-44`\n\n### 3.7 `keys.list handler` — invariant-change\n\nToday it runs one Keychain read per name; it now reads names and values through the vault. No in-repo client calls keys.list today.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474-1503`\n\n### 3.8 `Daemon boot` — invariant-change\n\nToday the daemon opens every registered repository before server.listen; that loop is removed, and closeDefaultManagedRoots stays registered for shutdown.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/daemon/index.ts:470-476`\n- `src/daemon/index.ts:539`\n\n## 4. Diagrams\n\n- [Sequence diagram](docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html)\n\n## 5. Error paths\n\n**Error cases**\n\n- **A save, delete or read arrives with a malformed name or value** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The runtime type check at the vault owner boundary fails\n  - Response: KeystoreInputError; the mutation queue is not entered and neither memory nor the Keychain changes.\n  - User impact: That request fails; other secrets stay readable.\n- **The user denies the Keychain dialog, or the Keychain read of the vault item fails** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: keytar.getPassword rejects during the single-flight vault load\n  - Response: Every waiting caller gets KeystoreUnavailableError with the cause. The failure is remembered for five minutes, in which reads fail at once without a dialog; the next read after that retries.\n  - User impact: Requests needing a secret report the connection unavailable with the cause; requests needing no secret continue.\n- **The vault item fails validation on load** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: JSON parsing, the version check or the whole-payload shape check fails after a successful Keychain read\n  - Response: Fail closed: KeystoreUnavailableError, the item is never rewritten and no legacy fallback is used, so a damaged item cannot be replaced by a partial one.\n  - User impact: Saved secrets are unavailable until the item is repaired or deliberately abandoned.\n- **A candidate payload fails validation before a write** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The same whole-payload check runs on the candidate inside the mutation queue\n  - Response: KeystoreUnavailableError; nothing is written and memory is unchanged.\n  - User impact: The save fails and the existing vault stays readable.\n- **The offline maintenance tool holds the vault guard when a daemon needs a secret** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: runFileGuardConflict reports the guard before the vault load\n  - Response: KeystoreUnavailableError naming the guard, with no Keychain access and no five-minute memory, so the first request after the guard is released succeeds.\n  - User impact: Requests needing a secret fail until maintenance ends; a crashed maintenance run leaves the guard for an operator to clear.\n- **The maintenance tool finds the daemon running after taking the guard** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The existing pid and socket absence check, now made after the guard is acquired, finds a file\n  - Response: The tool releases the guard and exits with its existing failure message, without touching the vault.\n  - User impact: Maintenance does not run; management stays disabled pending recovery as today.\n- **Writing the vault item fails on a save or delete** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: keytar.setPassword rejects inside the mutation queue\n  - Response: KeystoreUnavailableError to that caller; memory keeps its previous value, so memory and Keychain stay consistent.\n  - User impact: The save reports failure and the old value remains in force.\n- **Copying a legacy secret into the vault fails** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: keytar.setPassword rejects inside the mutation queue after the legacy read found a value\n  - Response: The value is kept as this run's cached value for the name and returned; the legacy item is untouched and the copy is retried on the next run.\n  - User impact: None this run; that name's legacy read on the next run can prompt again, an accepted exception under decision A.\n- **A legacy item read is refused during migration** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: keytar.getPassword on the legacy service rejects\n  - Response: KeystoreUnavailableError for that name only, remembered for five minutes per name; the vault and other names are unaffected.\n  - User impact: That connection is reported unavailable with the cause and is not re-prompted by each following request; the retry after five minutes can prompt again, an accepted exception under decision A.\n- **Opening a repository's saved connections fails on first use** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: ensureDefaultManagedRoot rejects with a keystore cause or an integrity failure\n  - Response: The rejected attempt is forgotten, the request gets 'secret-unavailable' for a keystore cause and 'recovery-required' otherwise; fresh initialization has written nothing if its ticket key could not be taken.\n  - User impact: That repository's request fails with its cause; the daemon and other repositories are unaffected.\n- **A worker's hub call to the vault owner fails or the channel closes** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The hub request rejects on the worker\n  - Response: KeystoreUnavailableError with the cause; the worker does not fall back to calling keytar itself.\n  - User impact: That request fails; no extra Keychain access occurs.\n\n**Edge cases**\n\n| Input | Expected |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| No vault item exists yet | keytar returns null with no dialog for a missing item; the vault starts empty and the item is created on the first write. |\n| A name exists nowhere, such as an unset web search key | getKey returns null; the absence is remembered for the run, not persisted, so a lookup causes no write. |\n| A save or delete lands while a legacy read for the same name is in flight | The save or delete wins; the copy finds the name in the vault or retired inside the mutation queue and is discarded. |\n| Two callers miss the same name at once | They share one legacy read and one copy. |\n| A name is deleted and an old legacy item for it remains | The retired list stops the legacy fallback, and getKey returns null with no legacy read. |\n| A retired name is saved again | setKey adds it to secrets and removes it from retired. |\n| An account name such as __proto__ or constructor | It is an ordinary key, because entries are held in a Map. |\n| An empty string as a secret value | It is a valid string and is stored; only a non-string value is refused. |\n| Many threads ask for different secrets while the first dialog is open | They wait on the one load; exactly one Keychain read of the vault occurs and requests needing no secret do not wait. |\n| daemon.threads.enabled is false | The main thread uses the vault directly with the same behaviour. |\n| A plain listing of a repository with no management marker | No state is created and the Keychain is not touched. |\n\n**Invariants to preserve**\n\n- getKey, setKey, deleteKey and listKeys keep their signatures, and the KeystoreLike port and its test seam keep working. [[c1]]\n- ensureDefaultManagedRoot stays memoised per root and forgets a failed attempt. [[c3]]\n- The CLI never opens the Keychain; only daemon code and the daemon-owned offline maintenance binary do. [[c4]]\n- Hub traffic stays in-process between the main thread and its workers. [[c5]]\n- A daemon shutdown still closes every root that was opened. [[c3]]\n\n## 6. Test strategy\n\n**Test framework:** `node:test`\n\n**Test levels**\n\n- **unit** — The vault's load, read, write, retire, validation, ordering and failure rules against a fake Keychain backend injected below the vault that counts calls.\n  - Subjects: `vault: concurrent reads perform one Keychain read`, `vault: a refused load fails at once for five minutes and then retries`, `vault: a payload with a bad version, missing secrets, a non-string value or a bad retired list fails closed and is never rewritten`, `vault: a malformed name or value leaves memory and the stored item unchanged`, `vault: a name such as __proto__ is stored and read as an ordinary key`, `vault: a failed write leaves memory unchanged`, `vault: concurrent saves lose no update`, `vault: a retired name does not fall back to its legacy item`, `vault: a retired name saved again is readable`, `migration: a legacy secret is copied once and read from the vault afterwards`, `migration: concurrent misses of one name share one legacy read and one copy`, `migration: a save during a legacy read wins and the copy is discarded`, `migration: a delete during a legacy read wins and the copy is discarded`, `migration: a failed copy serves later reads from memory, keeps the legacy item and reads it again on the next run`, `migration: an absent name causes no write and no second lookup in the run`, `migration: a refused legacy read fails at once for five minutes for that name only and then retries`, `keystore: listKeys never calls findCredentials`\n  - Fixtures: `A fake Keychain backend that counts reads and writes, can refuse them and can hold a read open, installed through a test-only setter below the vault`\n- **integration** — Thread ownership, process exclusion, on-demand opening and error mapping in real processes, with the fake backend installed below the vault in the process that owns it.\n  - Subjects: `threads: workers on two threads share one Keychain read`, `threads: a worker never calls the backend directly`, `threads: a closed hub channel does not fall back to the Keychain`, `threads: a save on one worker is visible on another`, `ipc: keys.set with a non-string value is refused and other secrets stay readable after a restart`, `guard: a daemon holding no vault fails requests while maintenance holds the guard and succeeds after release`, `guard: maintenance refuses and releases the guard when the daemon socket exists after acquiring it`, `boot: a daemon start reads nothing from the Keychain and opens its socket`, `on-demand: the first management request opens the repository and a later one does not reopen it`, `on-demand: a refused Keychain read reports secret-unavailable and the next request retries`, `on-demand: a refused first-time set-up leaves nothing on disk`, `on-demand: a plain listing of an unmanaged repository touches nothing`, `consumers: notify, web and keys handlers read through the vault`, `maintenance: the offline tool reads the vault once`\n  - Fixtures: `A node --import test preload that installs the fake backend in a spawned daemon or maintenance process, so no production switch is added, and that throws if the backend is called on a worker`, `A temporary repository with seeded saved connections`\n- **live** — The real macOS behaviour no fake can show, run by a person.\n  - Subjects: `live: after a node upgrade one dialog appears across several connections and threads once migration is complete`\n  - Fixtures: `A macOS login Keychain with several saved connections`\n\n**Acceptance mapping**\n\n| Criterion | Proving tests |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `ac1` | `boot: a daemon start reads nothing from the Keychain and opens its socket`, `on-demand: the first management request opens the repository and a later one does not reopen it`, `on-demand: a refused Keychain read reports secret-unavailable and the next request retries` |\n| `ac2` | `vault: concurrent reads perform one Keychain read`, `threads: workers on two threads share one Keychain read`, `threads: a save on one worker is visible on another`, `migration: a failed copy serves later reads from memory, keeps the legacy item and reads it again on the next run`, `migration: a refused legacy read fails at once for five minutes for that name only and then retries`, `live: after a node upgrade one dialog appears across several connections and threads once migration is complete` |\n| `ac3` | `consumers: notify, web and keys handlers read through the vault`, `maintenance: the offline tool reads the vault once`, `guard: a daemon holding no vault fails requests while maintenance holds the guard and succeeds after release` |\n| `ac4` | `migration: a legacy secret is copied once and read from the vault afterwards`, `migration: a save during a legacy read wins and the copy is discarded`, `migration: a delete during a legacy read wins and the copy is discarded`, `vault: a malformed name or value leaves memory and the stored item unchanged`, `ipc: keys.set with a non-string value is refused and other secrets stay readable after a restart` |\n\n## 7. Migration\n\n**State before:** Each secret is its own Keychain item under service 'insrc', read through keytar on every use (s1 symbol.locate), and main() opens every repository's saved connections before server.listen (s1 usage.example).\n\n**State after:** One vault item under service 'insrc-vault' holds every secret and is read once per daemon run by the main thread; saved connections open on first use. Legacy items remain until an explicit delete.\n\n**Zero downtime:** no — **Data rewrite:** no\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Ship the vault with the legacy fallback: a name absent from the vault, not retired and with no reusable run result is read from its legacy item and, when a value is found, copied in on first use. — ↩ rollbackable\n2. Remove the boot loop and open saved connections on first request. — ↩ rollbackable\n3. Each legacy secret is copied into the vault the first time it is used; a successful copy shows at most one dialog for that item and that name never reads its legacy item again. A failed copy or a denied dialog can prompt again on a later attempt (accepted exceptions, stakeholder decision A). No legacy item is deleted by migration. Once any secret has been saved or deleted through the vault, going back loses data, as step 4 states. — ✕ non-rollbackable\n4. Recovery if the vault must be abandoned: delete the single vault item, or run the previous daemon version; both read the untouched legacy items. This is not a clean rollback. A secret first saved after migration is lost and must be re-entered; a secret changed after migration reverts to its older legacy value; a secret deleted after migration whose best-effort legacy delete failed comes back and must be deleted again. — ✕ non-rollbackable\n\n**Backward compat:** getKey, setKey, deleteKey and listKeys keep their signatures and the KeystoreLike port and test seam are unchanged. A malformed name or value is now refused with KeystoreInputError where keytar refused it before. listKeys now reports vault names only, so a legacy item appears after first use; no in-repo client calls keys.list. A previous daemon version keeps reading legacy items and does not see the vault, with the losses stated in step 4.\n\n## 8. Alternatives considered\n\n### 8.1 a1: One Keychain item holding every secret, owned by the main thread — **CHOSEN**\n\nA JSON map of all secrets lives in one Keychain item under a new service; the main thread loads it once on first need and serves every thread from memory.\n\ngetKey, setKey, deleteKey and listKeys keep their signatures but use a vault: one Keychain item under a new service whose value is a versioned JSON map of name to secret. The first read loads it once, single-flight, and later reads come from memory. Workers forward over their existing hub channel, so only one thread touches the Keychain. The owner validates every name and value, and every change to the vault, including a migration copy, runs through one mutation queue that writes the item first and memory only after success. A name absent from the vault, not retired and with no reusable run result is read from its legacy item, single-flight per name, and a found value is copied in through that queue after re-checking the current state, so a stale copy cannot overwrite a save or undo a delete. Legacy items stay readable. The offline maintenance tool holds a cross-process guard for its whole run. The boot loop is removed and saved connections open on demand.\n\n### 8.2 a2: One Keychain master key with secrets in an encrypted file\n\nThe Keychain holds only an AES key; secrets live in an AES-GCM file under ~/.insrc, so saving a secret never touches the Keychain after the first read.\n\nThe vault keeps the same read and write surface and the same main-thread ownership, but its single Keychain item holds a random 256-bit key. Secrets are stored in one AES-GCM encrypted file written atomically under ~/.insrc; the key is read once per run and writes only re-encrypt the file. Migration and on-demand opening are as in a1.\n\n**Rejected because:** Removes the save dialog but moves secrets to a new encrypted store, and is only partial on lossless migration; the stakeholder declined it in decision A.\n\n### 8.3 a3: One Keychain item cached separately on each thread\n\nThe smallest change: the keystore module caches the single item in module scope, so each thread that needs a secret loads it for itself.\n\nThe keystore module holds the consolidated map in a module-level variable with no cross-thread forwarding. The main thread and each session worker load the item on their own first read and keep their own copy. Writes go to the Keychain and update only the writing thread's copy.\n\n**Rejected because:** Violates the one-prompt requirement: each thread does its own Keychain access and holds a stale copy after a write.\n\n## 9. References\n\n- **[[c1]]** `code` `src/shared/keystore.ts:10-40`\n- **[[c2]]** `code` `src/daemon/db/secrets.ts:26-44`\n- **[[c3]]** `code` `src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts`\n- **[[c4]]** `code` `src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts:14-30`\n- **[[c5]]** `code` `src/daemon/threads/channel.ts:117`\n- **[[c6]]** `code` `src/daemon/index.ts:470-476`\n- **[[c7]]** `code` `src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts:142-160`\n- **[[c8]]** `code` `src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts:64`\n- **[[c9]]** `prior-artifact` `ISSUE-fefa97b991537da7`\n- **[[c10]]** `prior-artifact` `LLD-669ae7a31701e106-S001`\n- **[[c11]]** `stakeholder` `Decision A, 2026-11-08` — \"Keep one Keychain item holding everything; accept that each legacy item prompts when successfully copied, that a failed copy or a denied dialog can prompt again on a later attempt, and that a save may\"\n"},"capturedAt":"2026-11-08T16:27:39.895Z"},"inventory":{"units":[{"id":"/body/summary","selector":"/body/summary","title":"summary","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/hldContextSlice","selector":"/body/hldContextSlice","title":"hldContextSlice","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/contractDetails","selector":"/body/contractDetails","title":"contractDetails","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/dataModelChanges","selector":"/body/dataModelChanges","title":"dataModelChanges","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/interactionWithShared","selector":"/body/interactionWithShared","title":"interactionWithShared","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/errorPaths","selector":"/body/errorPaths","title":"errorPaths","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/testStrategy","selector":"/body/testStrategy","title":"testStrategy","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/migration","selector":"/body/migration","title":"migration","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered","title":"alternativesConsidered","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/chosenAlternative","selector":"/body/chosenAlternative","title":"chosenAlternative","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/openQuestions","selector":"/body/openQuestions","title":"openQuestions","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition","selector":"/bod