44","src/daemon/db/pool.ts:290-301","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474-1503","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts:14-30"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Consider extending the planned manual macOS acceptance check to exercise saving after Allow versus Always Allow, alongside the existing post-migration read check, so decision A's save-prompt exception is observed directly."]},{"chunkId":"vault","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Owner-side validation and pre-write payload validation address the prior corruption risk. Migration ordering, retirement, retry qualifications and recovery losses are documented coherently. Two consumer contract inconsistencies remain.","findings":[{"id":"vault-r3-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/errorCases/10","message":"The worker error rule converts any rejected hub request into KeystoreUnavailableError, including an owner's KeystoreInputError for malformed arguments. This contradicts the get/set/delete input-error contracts and makes behavior depend on the calling thread. The existing hub preserves remote error names, so distinguish remote input rejection from transport failure, preserve the declared input error, and cover malformed worker requests in integration tests.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:46","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:69","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:92","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:261","src/daemon/threads/channel.ts:165"]},{"id":"vault-r3-002","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/errorPaths/edgeCases/7; /body/testStrategy","message":"Empty secret values are newly accepted explicitly, but the design leaves keys.get's truthiness check unchanged. Saving an empty string therefore succeeds while keys.get reports exists:false for that stored secret. Specify null-based existence checking for this consumer and add an empty-value IPC round-trip assertion.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:277","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1484","node_modules/keytar/lib/keytar.js:3 — the previous direct wrapper rejects empty passwords"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/1","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-fefa97b991537da7.json",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-669ae7a31701e106-S001.json: applicable keystore and migration constraints",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: prior vault-005 and current scope assessment","src/shared/keystore.ts:10-40","src/daemon/db/secrets.ts:26-44 and credential consumers","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474-1503","src/daemon/threads/channel.ts: hub error transport","src/daemon/tools/config.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/notify/index.ts: resolveSecretRef","src/daemon/tools/builtins/web/index.ts: keychain lookup","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts: guard APIs","node_modules/keytar/lib/keytar.js","node_modules/keytar/src/main.cc: argument validation","src, vscode-plugin and jetbrains-plugin: enumeration consumer searches"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Extend migration race tests to cover delayed legacy absence and rejection after a successful save or delete, alongside the planned found-value copy races."]},{"chunkId":"runtime","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The on-demand lifecycle, maintenance exclusion protocol and below-vault test fixtures are feasible against current code. One worker error-contract inconsistency remains: owner-side input rejection is specified to become an availability error on workers.","findings":[{"id":"runtime-r3-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/errorCases/10","message":"The worker rule maps every rejected hub request to KeystoreUnavailableError, which also includes the owner's KeystoreInputError for malformed arguments. This contradicts the get/set/delete contracts and gives identical requests different errors depending on their thread. Preserve remote input rejection separately from owner availability and transport failures, and cover malformed worker requests in the integration strategy. The existing hub already transports remote error names, so this distinction is implementable.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:46","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:69","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:92","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:261","src/daemon/threads/channel.ts: HubReply, HubRemoteError and HubClient reply reconstruction",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: body.testStrategy integration subjects"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/citations/0","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: assigned contracts, data model, shared interactions, errors, tests and citations","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/ISSUE.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-669ae7a31701e106-S001.json: applicable lifecycle, initialization ordering, integrity and error-mapping requirements",".insrc/tmp/design-review/rv-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: completed scope and vault feedback","src/shared/keystore.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts: acquireRunFileGuard, runFileGuardConflict and ownership-preserving release","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts","src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts: initialization, per-root memoization and shutdown","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts: integrity gates, rollback reads, enabled checks and cleanup","src/daemon/db/management-tickets.ts: SavedTicketAuthority.open","src/daemon/db/management.ts: managementRejection and savedManagementFor","src/daemon/db/secrets.ts: KeystoreLike and credentialKeystore indirection","src/daemon/connection-management-rpc.ts: owner, safeList, capabilities and management callers","src/daemon/db-rpc.ts: listing, saving and managed removal refusal","src/daemon/index.ts: boot loop, socket publication and shutdown ordering","src/daemon/server.ts: listen and close publication lifecycle","src/daemon/threads/channel.ts: hub payloads, remote errors and channel closure","src/daemon/threads/main-services.ts: connectWorker and serveHub installation","src/daemon/threads/worker-entry.ts: worker initialization and hub installation","src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts: connection and keys method classifications","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts: keys handlers","src/daemon/tools/config.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/notify/index.ts: resolveSecretRef","src/daemon/tools/builtins/web/index.ts: Keychain-backed Brave lookup","src/daemon/db/__tests__/management-defaults.test.ts","src/daemon/threads/__tests__/helpers/daemon-socket.ts: spawned daemon and IPC fixtures"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Add explicit integration assertions for threads-disabled operation and an unrelated request completing while a fake Keychain read remains pending.","Extend guard tests to cover concurrent maintenance admission, a crashed owner's retained guard, and rejection of maintenance while a daemon already holds a cached vault.","Clarify that the next management request retries the root opener immediately, while the underlying denied Keychain load remains subject to its five-minute cooldown."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"All assigned sequence and companion source units were inspected. The revised source addresses the substantive fallback and persistence conditions raised by visuals-001 and visuals-002. Two retained descriptions remain inaccurate. Mandatory rendered verification could not be completed because browser access is unavailable.","findings":[{"id":"visuals-r3-001","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/sequenceDefinition/messages/4/description","message":"The description says a remembered refusal never reaches legacy lookup, but refusals expire after five minutes and then permit another lookup. The companion repeats this wording. Qualify the exclusion as applying during the cooldown so the description agrees with the retry contract and accepted prompt exceptions.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: body.sequenceDefinition.messages[4].description","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/sequence-diagram.html: Messages table, step 5","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:166","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:253-256"]},{"id":"visuals-r3-002","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3/description","message":"The Keychain participant describes legacy items as held 'until copied', implying migration removes them. The migration contract explicitly retains these items after copying and removes them only on explicit deletion. Correct the participant description and regenerate its companion description.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1.json: body.sequenceDefinition.participants[3].description","docs/standalone/open-saved