,"src/daemon/db/management-defaults.ts","src/daemon/db/management-startup.ts","src/daemon/connection-management-rpc.ts:46-66","src/daemon/db-rpc.ts:79-170","src/daemon/db/secrets.ts:26-44","src/daemon/db/pool.ts:290-301","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1474-1503","src/bin/insrc-connection-maintenance.ts:14-30"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Consider extending the planned manual macOS acceptance check to exercise saving after Allow versus Always Allow, alongside the existing post-migration read check, so decision A's save-prompt exception is observed directly."]},{"chunkId":"vault","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Owner-side validation and pre-write payload validation address the prior corruption risk. Migration ordering, retirement, retry qualifications and recovery losses are documented coherently. Two consumer contract inconsistencies remain.","findings":[{"id":"vault-r3-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/errorCases/10","message":"The worker error rule converts any rejected hub request into KeystoreUnavailableError, including an owner's KeystoreInputError for malformed arguments. This contradicts the get/set/delete input-error contracts and makes behavior depend on the calling thread. The existing hub preserves remote error names, so distinguish remote input rejection from transport failure, preserve the declared input error, and cover malformed worker requests in integration tests.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:46","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:69","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:92","docs/standalone/open-saved-connections-demand-read-all-E20261104fefa97b9/S001/LLD.md:261","src/daemon/threads/channel.ts:165"]},{"id":"vault-r3-002","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/errorPaths/edgeCases/7; /body/testStrategy","message":"Empty secret values are newly accepted 