1403	{"artifactId":"LLD-fefa97b991537da7-s1","entry":{"id":"15d512f70b11420386a8d2f7f3980eed","actor":{"id":"insrc:approval","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-08T16:45:46.199Z","operation":"approve","revision":{"number":3,"contentHash":"2197be84be4ab974a30e97cf19b78bb1c236cdb6613e5fb5c0240c1d305cb585"},"status":{"from":"draft","to":"approved"},"outcome":{"result":"override","summary":"User chose override after three design review rounds (2 HIGH resolved). Conditions on the build: (1) a worker must preserve the owner's KeystoreInputError for malformed requests and map only availability and transport failures to KeystoreUnavailableError, with an integration test for a malformed worker request (MED vault-r3-001 / runtime-r3-001); (2) keys.get must use a null check so an empty saved secret reports exists:true, with an IPC round-trip assertion (LOW vault-r3-002); (3) the sequence notes must say a remembered refusal applies during the five-minute cooldown, and that legacy items are retained after copying (LOW visuals-r3-001, visuals-r3-002). The remaining MEDs, visuals-001 and visuals-002, are carried only because the reviewer's browser host was unavailable; the reviewer found the source corrected, and the diagram was rendered in headless Chrome on 2026-11-08 and drew all nine steps with the corrected conditions, the Keychain column needing Fit or pan at default zoom."}}}
